225 1606 1702 (    From a transient programs perspective, Bank 1 is always in context.  The operating) 1702 SB
225 1665 1606 (   system can switch to Bank 0 or other banks when performing operating system) 1606 SB
225 1724 1735 (   functions without affecting.the execution of the transient program.  Any bank-switch-) 1735 SB
225 1784 1678 (   ing performed by the operating system is completely transparent to the calling pro-) 1678 SB
225 1843 1737 (   gram.  Because the major portion of the operating system resides in Bank 0 in banked) 1737 SB
225 1902 1677 (   systems, more memory space is available for transient programs in banked CP/M 3) 1677 SB
225 1961 749 (   systems than in nonbanked systems.) 749 SB
225 2079 1633 (    The operating system uses the clear areas in Figures 1-2 and 1-3 for disk record) 1633 SB
