225 227 1670 (          The banked version of CP/M 3 requires a minimum of two banks, Bank 0 and) 1670 SB
225 286 1715 (        Bank 1, and can support up to 16 banks of memory.  Bank numbers are generally) 1715 SB
225 345 1753 (        arbitrary with the following exceptions: Bank 0 is the system bank and is in context) 1753 SB
225 405 1763 (        when CP/M 3 is started.  Bank 1 is the transient program bank, and must be contig-) 1763 SB
225 464 1729 (        uous from location zero to the top of banked memory.  This requirement does not) 1729 SB
225 523 1591 (        apply to the other banks.  However, common memory must be contiguous.) 1591 SB
225 641 1758 (          The size of the common region is typically 16K.  The only size requirement on the) 1758 SB
225 700 1767 (        common region is that it must be large enough to contain the resident portion of the) 1767 SB
225 760 1749 (        operating system.  The maximum top of memory address for both banked and non-) 1749 SB
225 819 837 (        banked systems is 64K-1 \(OFFFFH\).) 837 SB
225 937 1733 (          In summary, no matter how physical memory is configured, or whether the oper-) 1733 SB
225 996 1778 (        ating system is banked or nonbanked, CP/M 3 always organizes memory logically so) 1778 SB
225 1055 1681 (        that to a transient program in any CP/M 3 system, memory appears as shown in) 1681 SB
225 1115 325 (        Figure 1-4.) 325 SB
