547 1240 1306 (Figure 1-5.  System Components and Regions in Logical Memory) 1306 SB
225 1358 1759 (      The Basic Input/Output System, BIOS, is a hardware-dependent module that defines) 1759 SB
225 1418 1739 (   the low-level interface to a particular computer system.  It contains the device-driving) 1739 SB
225 1477 917 (   routines necessary for peripheral device I/O.) 917 SB
225 1595 1743 (      The Basic Disk Operating System, BDOS, is the hardware-independent module that) 1743 SB
225 1654 1664 (   is the logical nucleus of CP/M 3. It provides a standard operating environment for) 1664 SB
225 1713 1685 (   transient programs by making services available through numbered system function) 1685 SB
225 1773 139 (   calls.) 139 SB
225 1891 1732 (      The LOADER module handles program loading for the Console Command Proces-) 1732 SB
225 1950 1704 (   sor and transient programs.  Usually, this module is not resident when transient pro-) 1704 SB
225 2009 1631 (   grams execute.  However, when it is resident, transient programs can access this) 1631 SB
225 2068 914 (   module by making BDOS Function 59 calls.) 914 SB
225 2187 1648 (      Resident System Extensions, RSXS, are temporary additional operating system) 1648 SB
225 2246 1653 (   modules that can selectively extend or modify normal operating system functions.) 1653 SB
225 2305 1315 (   The LOADER module is always resident when RSXs are active.) 1315 SB
1166 2838 67 (1-6) 67 SB
225 92 1946 ( 1.2 System Components                                                                  CP/M 3 Programmer's Guide ) 1946 SB
