225 227 772 (     1.3.2 Applications and the BDOS) 772 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 1708 (       Transient programs and the CCP access CP/M 3 facilities by making BDOS func-) 1708 SB
225 405 1771 (     tion calls.  BDOS functions can create, delete, open, and close disk files, read or write) 1771 SB
225 464 1672 (     to opened files, retrieve input from the console, send output to the console or list) 1672 SB
225 523 1684 (     device, and perform a wide range of other services described in Section 3,"BDOS) 1684 SB
225 582 292 (     Functions.") 292 SB
225 700 1626 (       To make a BDOS function call, a transient program loads CPU registers with) 1626 SB
225 760 1683 (     specific entry parameters and calls location 0005H in Page Zero.  If RSXs are not) 1683 SB
225 819 1514 (     active in memory, location 0005H contains a jump instruction to location) 1514 SB

