225 878 1716 (     BDOS_base + 6. If RSXs are active, location 0005H contains a jump instruction to) 1716 SB
225 937 1783 (     an address below BDOS   -base. Thus, the Page Zero interface allows programs to run) 1783 SB
225 996 1684 (     without regard to where the operating system modules are located in memory.  In) 1684 SB
225 1055 1654 (     addition, transient programs can use the address at location 0006H as a memory) 1654 SB
225 1115 207 (     ceiling.) 207 SB
225 1233 1717 (       Some BDOS functions are similar to BIOS entry points, particularly in the case of) 1717 SB
225 1292 1711 (     simple device I/O.  For example, when a transient program makes a console output) 1711 SB
225 1351 1777 (     BDOS function call, the BDOS makes a BIOS console output call.  In the case of disk) 1777 SB
225 1410 1723 (     I/O, however, this relationship is more complex.  The BDOS might call many BIOS) 1723 SB
225 1470 1177 (     entry points to perform a single BDOS file I/O function.) 1177 SB
225 1588 1738 (       Transient programs can terminate execution by jumping to location OOOOH in the) 1738 SB
225 1647 1732 (     Page Zero region.  This location contains a jump instruction to BIOS base+3, which) 1732 SB
225 1706 1704 (     contains a jump instruction to the BIOS warm start routine.  The BIOS warm start) 1704 SB
225 1765 1698 (     routine loads the CCP into memory at location 100H and then passes control to it.) 1698 SB
225 1884 1721 (       The Console Command Processor is a special system program that executes in the) 1721 SB
225 1943 1756 (     TPA and makes BDOS calls 'ust like an application program.  However, the CCP has) 1756 SB
225 2002 1682 (     a unique role: it gives the user access to operating system facilities while transient) 1682 SB
225 2061 1777 (     programs are not executing.  It includes several built-in commands, such as TYPE and) 1777 SB
225 2120 1743 (     DIR, that can be executed directly without having to be loaded from disk.  When the) 1743 SB
225 2180 1738 (     CCP receives control, it reads the uscr's command lines, distinguishes between built-) 1738 SB
225 2239 1740 (     in and transient commands, and when necessary, calls upon the LOADER module to) 1740 SB
225 2298 1780 (     load transient programs from disk into the TPA for execution.  Section 1.6.2 describes) 1780 SB
225 2357 544 (     CCP operation in detail.) 544 SB
1166 2830 67 (1-8) 67 SB
