225 227 700 (       1.3.3 Applications and RSXs) 700 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 1730 (         A Resident System Extension is a temporary additional operating system module.) 1730 SB
225 405 1724 (       An RSX can extend or modify one or more operating system functions selectively.) 1724 SB
225 464 1722 (       As with a standard BDOS function, a transient program accesses an RSX function) 1722 SB
225 523 761 (       through a numbered function call.) 761 SB
225 641 1667 (         At any one time there might be zero, one, or multiple RSXs active in memory.) 1667 SB
225 700 1729 (       When a transient program makes a BDOS function call, and RSXs are active, each) 1729 SB
225 760 1735 (       RSX examines the function number of the call.  If the function number matches the) 1735 SB
225 819 1742 (       function the RSX is designed to extend or modify, the RSX performs the requested) 1742 SB
225 878 1808 (       function.  Otherwise, the RSX passes the function request to the next RSX.  Noninter-) 1808 SB
225 937 1595 (       ceptcd functions are eventually passed to the BDOS for standard execution.) 1595 SB
225 1055 1720 (         RSXs are loaded into memory when programs containing RSXs are loaded.  The) 1720 SB
225 1115 1802 (       CP/M 3 utility, GENCOM, can attach RSXs to program files.  When attaching RSXS,) 1802 SB
225 1174 1790 (       GENCOM places a special one page header at the beginning of the program file.  The) 1790 SB
225 1233 1792 (       CCP reads this header, learns that a program has attached RSXS, and loads the RSXs) 1792 SB
225 1292 1735 (       accordingly.  The header itself is not loaded into memory; it merely indicates to the) 1735 SB
225 1351 778 (       CCP that RSX loading is required.) 778 SB
225 1470 1727 (         The LOADER module is a special type of RSX that supports BDOS function 59,) 1727 SB
225 1529 1784 (       Load Overlay.  It is always resident when RSXs are active.  To indicate RSX support) 1784 SB
225 1588 1726 (       is required, a program that calls function 59 must have an RSX header attached by) 1726 SB
225 1647 1648 (       GENCOM, even if the program does not require other RSXS.  When the CCP) 1648 SB
225 1706 1757 (       encounters this type of header in a program file when no RSXs are active, it sets the) 1757 SB
225 1765 1535 (       address at location 0006H in Page Zero to LOADER-base + 6 instead of) 1535 SB
225 1825 428 (       BDOS_base + 6.) 428 SB
