225 227 1689 (          The size of the BDOS region differs for the banked and nonbanked versions of) 1689 SB
225 286 1677 (        CP/M 3. In the banked version, the resident BDOS size is 6 pages, 1.5K. In the) 1677 SB
225 345 1795 (        nonbanked system, the BDOS size ranges from 31 pages, 7.75K, to 33 pages, 8.25K,) 1795 SB
225 405 1395 (        depending on system generation options and BIOS requirements.) 1395 SB
225 523 1770 (          RSXs are page aligned modules that are stacked in memory below LOADER_base) 1770 SB
225 582 1765 (        in memory.  In the configuration shown in Figure 1-6, location 0005H of Page Zero) 1765 SB
225 641 1776 (        contains a jump to location RSX\(N\)_base + 6. Thus, the memory ceiling of the TPA) 1776 SB
225 700 910 (        region is reduced when RSXs are active.) 910 SB
225 819 1740 (          Under CP/M 3. the CCP is a transient program that the BIOS loads into the TPA) 1740 SB
225 878 1805 (        region of memory at system cold and warm start.  The BIOS also loads the LOADER) 1805 SB
225 937 1801 (        module at this time, because the LOADER module is attached to the CCP.  When the) 1801 SB
225 996 1737 (        CCP gains control, it relocates the LOADER module just below BDOS_base. The) 1737 SB
225 1055 1686 (        LOADER module handles program loading for the CCP.  It is three pages long.) 1686 SB
225 1174 1650 (          The maximum size of a transient program that can be loaded into the TPA Is) 1650 SB
225 1233 1758 (        limited by LOADER-base because the LOADER cannot load a program over itself.) 1758 SB
225 1292 1780 (        Transient programs may extend beyond this point, however, by using memory above) 1780 SB
225 1351 1768 (        LOADER   - base for uninitialized data areas such as I/O buffers. Programs that use) 1768 SB
225 1410 1347 (        memory above BDOS-base cannot make BDOS function calls.) 1347 SB
