225 1647 1773 (          CP/M 3 can support up to sixteen logical drives, identified by the letters A through) 1773 SB
225 1706 1796 (        PI, with up to 512 megabytes of storage each.  A logical drive usually corresponds to) 1796 SB
225 1765 1753 (        a physical drive on the system, particularly for physical drives that support remova-) 1753 SB
225 1825 1736 (        ble media such as floppy disks.  High-capacity hard disks, however, are commonly) 1736 SB
225 1884 1757 (        divided up into multiple logical drives.  Figure 1-7 illustrates the standard organiza-) 1757 SB
225 1943 547 (        tion of a CP/M 3 disk.) 547 SB
1154 2830 92 (1-11) 92 SB
