225 996 1649 (        question marks, ????????.???, equals an ambiguous reference of two asterisks,) 1649 SB
225 1055 1605 (        and matches all files in the directory that belong to the current user number.) 1605 SB
225 1174 1777 (          The CP/M 3 file system automatically allocates directory space and data area space) 1777 SB
225 1233 1693 (        when a file is created or extended, and returns previously allocated space to free) 1693 SB
225 1292 1800 (        space when a file is deleted or truncated.  If no directory or data space is available for) 1800 SB
225 1351 1791 (        a requested operation, the BDOS returns an error to the calling program.  In general,) 1791 SB
225 1410 1723 (        the allocation and deallocation of disk space is transparent to the calling program.) 1723 SB
225 1470 1744 (        As a result, you need not be concerned with directory and drive organization when) 1744 SB
225 1529 918 (        using the file system facilities of CP/M 3.) 918 SB
