225 1765 1697 (          This section introduces the general operation of CP/M 3. This overview covers) 1697 SB
225 1825 1749 (        opics concerning the CP/M 3 system components, how they function and how they) 1749 SB
225 1884 1757 (        interact when CP/M 3 is running.  This section does not describe the total function-) 1757 SB
225 1943 1379 (        ality of CP/M 3, but simply introduces basic CP/M 3 operations.) 1379 SB
225 2061 1690 (          For the purpose of this overview, CP/M 3 system operation is divided into five) 1690 SB
225 2120 1794 (        categories.  First is system cold start, the process that begins execution of the operat-) 1794 SB
225 2180 1726 (        ing system.  This procedure ends when the Console Command Processor, CCP, is) 1726 SB
225 2239 1787 (        loaded into memory and the system prompt is displayed on the screen.  Second is the) 1787 SB
225 2298 1795 (        operation of the CCP, which provides the user interface to CP/M 3. Third is transient) 1795 SB
225 2357 1728 (        program initiation, execution and termination.  Fourth is the way Resident System) 1728 SB
225 2416 1782 (        Ex,ensions run under CP/M 3. The fifth and final category describes the operation of) 1782 SB
225 2475 677 (        the CP/M 3 SUBMIT utility.) 677 SB
1154 2830 92 (1-13) 92 SB
225 92 1913 (1.5 Disk Organization                                                                     CP/M 3 Programmer's Guide) 1913 SB
EJ RS
