225 227 500 (    1.6.2 CCP Operation) 500 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 1648 (      The Console Command Processor provides the user access to CP/M 3 facilities) 1648 SB
225 405 1657 (    when transient programs are not running.  It also reads the user's command lines,) 1657 SB
225 464 1713 (    differentiates between built-in commands and transient commands, and executes the) 1713 SB
225 523 520 (    commands accordingly.) 520 SB
225 641 1608 (      This section describes the responsibilities and capabilities of the CCP in some) 1608 SB
225 700 1635 (    detail.  The section begins with a description of the CCP's activities when it first) 1635 SB
225 760 1745 (    receives control from the Cold Start procedure.  The section continues with a general) 1745 SB
225 819 1672 (    discussion of built-in commands, and concludes with a step-by-step description of) 1672 SB
225 878 1321 (    the procedure the CCP follows to execute the user's commands.) 1321 SB
225 996 1591 (      When the CCP gains control following a cold start procedure, it displays the) 1591 SB
225 1055 1621 (    system prompt at the console.  This signifies that the CCP is ready to execute a) 1621 SB
225 1115 1742 (    command.  The system prompt displays the letter of the drive designated as the initial) 1742 SB
225 1174 1696 (    default drive during GENCPM operation.  For example, if drive A was specified as) 1696 SB
225 1233 1308 (    the initial default drive, the CCP displays the following prompt:) 1308 SB

