225 1351 128 (    A >) 128 SB
225 1470 1717 (    After displaying the system prompt, the CCP scans the directory of the default drive) 1717 SB
225 1529 1622 (    for the file PROFILE.SUB. If the file exists, the CCP creates the command line) 1622 SB
225 1588 1725 (    SUBMIT PROFILE; otherwise the CCP reads the user's first command line by mak-) 1725 SB
225 1647 1425 (    ing a BDOS Read Console Buffer function call \(BDOS Function 10\).) 1425 SB
225 1765 1736 (      The CCP accepts two different command forms.  The simplest CCP command form) 1736 SB
225 1825 1639 (    changes the default drive.  The following example illustrates a user changing the) 1639 SB
225 1884 570 (    default drive from A to B.) 570 SB
225 2002 162 (    A>B:) 162 SB
225 2061 126 (    B >) 126 SB
225 2180 1694 (    This command is one of the CCP's built-in commands.  Built-in commands are part) 1694 SB
225 2239 1671 (    of the CCP.  They reside in memory while the CCP is active, and therefore can be) 1671 SB
225 2298 772 (    executed without referencing a disk.) 772 SB
