225 227 1676 (      The command field must identify either a built-in command, a transient program,) 1676 SB
225 286 1717 (    or a submit file.  For example, USER is the keyword that identifies the built-in com-) 1717 SB
225 345 1640 (    mand that changes the current user number.  The CP/M 3 CCP displays the user) 1640 SB
225 405 1633 (    number in the system prompt when the user number is non-zero.  The following) 1633 SB
225 464 1280 (    example illustrates changing the user number from zero to 15.) 1280 SB
225 582 304 (    B>USER 15) 304 SB
