225 2120 1677 (       Some built-in commands have associated command files which expand upon the) 1677 SB
225 2180 1660 (    options provided by the built-in command.  If the CCP reads a command line and) 1660 SB
225 2239 1697 (    discovers the built-in command does not support the options requested in the com-) 1697 SB
225 2298 1629 (    mand line,, the CCP loads the built-in function's corresponding command file to) 1629 SB
225 2357 1700 (    perform the command.  The DIR command is an example of this type of command.) 1700 SB
225 2416 1675 (    Simple DIR commands are supported by the DIR built-in directly.  More complex) 1675 SB
225 2475 956 (    requests are handled by the DIR.COM utility.) 956 SB
