0 0 0 fC
225 227 1731 (            If the command field is preceded by a drive specification id:\), the CCP attempts) 1731 SB
225 286 1628 (            to open the command or submit file on the specified drive.  Otherwise, the) 1628 SB
225 345 1567 (            CCP attempts to open the file on the drives specified in the drive chain.) 1567 SB
225 405 1729 (            The drive chain specifies up to four drives that are to be referenced in sequence) 1729 SB
225 464 1676 (            for CCP open operations of command and submit files.  If an open operation) 1676 SB
225 523 1676 (            is unsuccessful on a drive in the drive chain because the file cannot be found,) 1676 SB
225 582 1578 (            the CCP repeats the open operation on the next drive in the chain.  This) 1578 SB
225 641 1626 (            sequence of open operations is repeated until the file is found, or the drive) 1626 SB
225 700 1642 (            chain is exhausted.  The drive chain contains the current default drive as its) 1642 SB
225 760 1684 (            only drive unless the user modifies the drive chain with the CP/M 3 SETDEF) 1684 SB
225 819 283 (            utility.) 283 SB
225 937 1685 (            When the current user number is non-zero, all open requests that fail because) 1685 SB
225 996 1676 (            the file cannot be found, attempt to locate the command file under user zero.) 1676 SB
225 1055 1558 (            If the file exists under user zero with the system attribute set, the file is) 1558 SB
225 1115 1667 (            opened from user zero.  This search for a file under user zero is made by the) 1667 SB
225 1174 1668 (            BDOS Open File function.  Thus, the user zero open attempt is made before) 1668 SB
225 1233 1087 (            advancing to the next drive in the search chain.) 1087 SB
225 1292 1649 (            When automatic submit is in effect, the CCP attempts to open with the first) 1649 SB
225 1351 1595 (            filetype, SUB or COM, on all drives in the search chain before trying the) 1595 SB
225 1410 466 (            second filetype.) 466 SB
225 1529 1662 (            In the banked system, if a password specified in the command field does not) 1662 SB
225 1588 1664 (            match the password of a file on a disk protected in Read mode, the CCP file) 1664 SB
225 1647 1185 (            open operation is terminated with a password error.) 1185 SB
225 1706 1677 (            If the CCP does not find the command or submit file, it echoes the command) 1677 SB
225 1765 1629 (            line followed by a question mark to the console.  If it finds a command file) 1629 SB
225 1825 1589 (            with a filetype of COM or PRL, the CCP proceeds to step 4. If it finds a) 1589 SB
225 1884 1672 (            submit file, it reconstructs the command line as described above, and repeats) 1672 SB
225 1943 980 (            step 3 for the command, SUBMIT.COM.) 980 SB
1154 2830 92 (1-20) 92 SB
