225 227 1742 (             4.  When the CCP successfully opens the command file, it initializes the follow-) 1742 SB
225 286 1486 (                 ing Page Zero fields for access by the loaded transient program:) 1486 SB
225 345 1306 (                 0050H    Drive that the command file was loaded from) 1306 SB
225 405 1311 (                 0051H    Password address of first file in command tail) 1311 SB
225 464 1284 (                 0053H    Password length of first file in command tail) 1284 SB
225 523 1371 (                 0054H    Password address of second file in command tail) 1371 SB
225 582 1344 (                 0056H    Password length of second file in command tail) 1344 SB
225 641 1221 (                 005CH    Parsed FCB for first file in command tail) 1221 SB
225 700 1281 (                 006CH    Parsed FCB for second file in command tail) 1281 SB
225 760 1355 (                 0080H    Command tail preceded by command tail length) 1355 SB
225 878 1481 (                 Page Zero initialization is covered in more detail in Section 2.4.) 1481 SB
225 996 1729 (             5.  At this point, the CCP calls the LOADER module to load the command file) 1729 SB
225 1055 1735 (                 into the TPA.  The LOADER module terminates the load operation if a read) 1735 SB
225 1115 1740 (                 error occurs, or if the available TPA space is not large enough to contain the) 1740 SB
225 1174 1689 (                 file.  If no RSXs are resident in memory, the available TPA space is deter-) 1689 SB
225 1233 1823 (                 mined by the address LOADER    - base because the LOADER cannot load over) 1823 SB
225 1292 1795 (                 itself.  Otherwise, the maximum TPA address is determined by the base address) 1795 SB
225 1351 826 (                 of the lowest RSX in memory.) 826 SB
225 1470 1751 (             6.  Once the program is loaded, the LOADER module checks for a RSX header) 1751 SB
225 1529 1630 (                 on the program.  Programs with RSX headers are identified by a return) 1630 SB
225 1588 791 (                 instruction at location 100H.) 791 SB
225 1706 1755 (                 If an RSX header is present, the LOADER relocates all RSXs attached to the) 1755 SB
225 1765 1625 (                 end of the program, to the top of the TPA region of memory under the) 1625 SB
225 1825 1796 (                 LOADER module, or any other RSXs that are already resident.  It also updates) 1796 SB
225 1884 1678 (                 the address in location 0006H of Page Zero to address the lowest RSX in) 1678 SB
225 1943 1706 (                 memory.  Finally, the LOADER discards the RSX header and relocates the) 1706 SB
225 2002 1703 (                 program file down one page in memory so that the first executable instruc-) 1703 SB
225 2061 634 (                 tion resides at 100H.) 634 SB
225 2180 1699 (             7.  After initializing Page Zero, the LOADER module sets up a 32-byte stack) 1699 SB
225 2239 1706 (                 with the return address set to location OOOOH of Page Zero and jumps to) 1706 SB
225 2298 1745 (                 location 100H.  At this point, the loaded transient program begins execution.) 1745 SB
1154 2830 92 (1-21) 92 SB
225 92 1907 (1.6 System Operation                                                                     CP/M 3 Programmer's Guide) 1907 SB
