0 0 0 fC
225 227 1743 (           A transient program can terminate execution in one of three ways: by jumping to) 1743 SB
225 286 1808 (          location 0000H, by making a BDOS System Reset call, or by making a BDOS Chain) 1808 SB
225 345 1839 (          To Program call.  The first two methods are equivalent; they pass control to the BIOS) 1839 SB
225 405 1661 (          warm start entry point, which then loads the CCP into the TPA, and the CCP) 1661 SB
225 464 756 (          prompts for the next command.) 756 SB
225 582 1700 (           The Chain to Program call allows a transient program to specify the next com-) 1700 SB
225 641 1769 (          mand to be executed before it terminates its own execution.  A Program Chain call) 1769 SB
225 700 1771 (          executes a standard warm boot sequence, but passes the command specified by the) 1771 SB
225 760 1768 (          terminating program to the CCP in such a way that the CCP executes the specified) 1768 SB
225 819 1448 (          command instead of prompting the console for the next command.) 1448 SB
225 937 1697 (           Transient programs can also set a Program Return Code before terminating by) 1697 SB
225 996 1806 (          making a BDOS Function 108 call, Get/Set Program Return Code.  The CCP initial-) 1806 SB
225 1055 1814 (          izes the Program Return Code to zero, successful, when it loads a transient program,) 1814 SB
225 1115 1801 (          unless the program is loaded as the result of a program chain.  Therefore, a transient) 1801 SB
225 1174 1728 (          program that terminates successfully can use the Program Return Code to pass a) 1728 SB
225 1233 1800 (          value to a chained program.  If the program terminates as the result of a BDOS fatal) 1800 SB
225 1292 1720 (          error, or a CTRL-C entered at the console, the BDOS sets the return code to an) 1720 SB
225 1351 1784 (          unsuccessful value.  All other types of program termination leave the return code at) 1784 SB
225 1410 462 (          its current value.) 462 SB
225 1529 1752 (           The CCP has a conditional command facility that uses the Program Return Code.) 1752 SB
225 1588 1801 (          If a command line submitted to the CCP by the SUBMIT utility begins with a colon,) 1801 SB
225 1647 1808 (          the CCP skips execution of the command if the previous command set an unsuccess-) 1808 SB
225 1706 1740 (          ful Program Return Code.  In the following example, the SUBMIT utility sends a) 1740 SB
225 1765 766 (          command sequence to the CCP:) 766 SB
225 1884 597 (          A>SUBMIT SUBFILE) 597 SB
225 1943 777 (          A>COMPUTE RESULTS.DAT) 777 SB
225 2002 796 (          A >: REPORT RESULTS. DA T) 796 SB
225 2120 1792 (          The CCP does not execute the REPORT command if the COMPUTE command ses) 1792 SB
225 2180 904 (          an unsuccessful Program Return Code.) 904 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c34a font
225 2298 1050 (          1.6.4 Resident System Extension Operation) 1050 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 2416 1749 (            This section gives a general overview of RSX use, then describes how RSXs are) 1749 SB
225 2475 1784 (          loaded, defines the RSX file structure, and tells how the LOADER module uses the) 1784 SB
225 2535 1045 (          RSX prefix and flags to manage RSX activity.) 1045 SB
1154 2830 92 (1-23) 92 SB
225 92 1907 (1.6 System Operation                                                                     CP/M 3 Programmer's Guide) 1907 SB
