0 0 0 fC
225 227 1729 (      When the CCP gains control after a system warm       start, it removes any RSXs in) 1729 SB
225 286 1678 (    memory that have the Remove flag set to OFFH.  All other RSXs remain active in) 1678 SB
225 345 1758 (    memory.  Setting an RSX's Remove flag to OFFH indicates that the RSX is not active) 1758 SB
225 405 1799 (    and it can be removed.  Note that if an RSX marked for removal is not the lowest active) 1799 SB
225 464 1742 (    RSX in memory, it still occupies memory after removal.  Although the removed RSX) 1742 SB
225 523 1767 (    cannot be executed, its space is returned to the TPA only when all the lower RSXs are) 1767 SB
225 582 238 (    removed.) 238 SB
225 700 1755 (      There 'is one special case where the CCP does not remove an RSX with the Remove) 1755 SB
225 760 1765 (    flag set to OFFH following warm start.  This case occurs on warm starts following the) 1765 SB
225 819 1690 (    load of an empty file with attached RSXS.  This exception allows an RSX with the) 1690 SB
225 878 1749 (    Remove flag set to be loaded into i-nemory before a transient program.  The transient) 1749 SB
225 937 1651 (    program can then access the RSX during execution.  After the transient program) 1651 SB
225 996 1615 (    terminates, however, the CCP removes the RSX from the system environment.) 1615 SB
225 1115 1725 (      As an example of RSX operation, here is a description of the operation of the GET) 1725 SB
225 1174 1710 (     utility.  The GET.COM command file has an attached RSX.  The LOADER moves) 1710 SB
225 1233 1657 (    this RSX to the top of the TPA when it loads the GET.COM command file.  The) 1657 SB
225 1292 1693 (    GET utility performs necessary initializations which include opening the ASCII file) 1693 SB
225 1351 1617 (    specified in the GET command line.  It also makes a BDOS Function 60 call to) 1617 SB
225 1410 1719 (    initialize the GET.RSX. At this point, the GET utility terminates.  Subsequently, the) 1719 SB
225 1470 1740 (    GET.RSX intercepts all console input calls and returns characters from the file speci-) 1740 SB
225 1529 1707 (    fied in the GET command line.  It continues this action until it reads end-of-file.  At) 1707 SB
225 1588 1688 (    this point, it sets its Remove flag in the RSX prefix, and stops intercepting console) 1688 SB
225 1647 1610 (    input.  On the following warm boot, the CCP removes the RSX from memory.) 1610 SB
