225 286 1736 (         <filespec> and creates a temporary submit file of type $$$ on the system's tempo-) 1736 SB
225 345 1722 (         rary file drive.  GENCPM initializes the temporary file drive to the CCP's current) 1722 SB
225 405 1811 (         default drive.  The SETDEF utility can set the temporary file drive to a specific drive.) 1811 SB
225 464 1888 (         As it creates the temporary file, SUBMIT performs the parameter substitutions requested) 1888 SB
225 523 1725 (         by the <parameters> subfield of the SUBMIT command line.  See the CP/M Plus) 1725 SB
225 582 1755 (         \(CP/M Version 3\) Operating System User's Guide for a detailed description of this) 1755 SB
225 641 280 (         process.) 280 SB
225 760 1770 (           After SUBMIT creates the temporary submit file, its operation is similar to that of) 1770 SB
225 819 1756 (         the GET utility described in Section 1.6.4. The SUBMIT command file also has an) 1756 SB
225 878 1705 (         attached RSX that performs console input redirection from a file.  However, the) 1705 SB
225 937 1806 (         SUBMIT RSX expands upon the simpler facilities provided by the GET RSX.  Com-) 1806 SB
225 996 1734 (         mand lines in a submit file can be marked to indicate whether they are program or) 1734 SB
225 1055 1792 (         CCP input.  Furthermore, if a program exhausts all its program input, the next SUB-) 1792 SB
225 1115 1814 (         MIT command is a CCP command, the SUBMIT RSX temporarily reverts to console) 1814 SB
225 1174 1767 (         input.  Redirected input from the submit file resumes when the program terminates.) 1767 SB
225 1292 1735 (           Because CP/M 3's submit facility is implemented with RSXS, submit files can be) 1735 SB
225 1351 1744 (         nested.  That is\) a submit file can contain additional SUBMIT or GET commands.) 1744 SB
225 1410 1748 (         Similarly, a GET command can specify a file that contains GET or SUBMIT com-) 1748 SB
225 1470 1757 (         mands.  For example, when a SUBMIT command is encountered in a submit file, a) 1757 SB
225 1529 1831 (         new SUBMIT RSX is created below the current RSX.  The new RSX handles console) 1831 SB
225 1588 1710 (         input until it reads end-of-file on its temporary submit file.  At this point, control) 1710 SB
225 1647 889 (         reverts to the previous SUBMIT RSX.) 889 SB
