225 1174 640 (    2.2 BDOS Serial Device I/O) 640 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 1292 1710 (      Under CP/M 3, serial device I/O is simply input to and output from simple devices) 1710 SB
225 1351 1719 (    such as consoles, line printers, and communications devices.  These physical devices) 1719 SB
225 1410 1160 (    can be assigned the logical device names defined below:) 1160 SB
225 1529 367 (        CONIN:       ) 367 SB
675 1529 549 (logical console input device) 549 SB
225 1588 378 (        CONOUT:    ) 378 SB
675 1588 579 (logical console output device) 579 SB
225 1647 382 (        AUXIN:        ) 382 SB
675 1647 567 (logical auxiliary input device) 567 SB
225 1706 380 (        AUXOUT:    ) 380 SB
675 1706 597 (logical auxiliary output device) 597 SB
225 1765 324 (        LST:         ) 324 SB
675 1765 486 (logical list output device) 486 SB
225 1884 1714 (      If your system supports the BIOS DEVTBL function, the CP/M 3 DEVICE utility) 1714 SB
225 1943 1778 (    can display and change the assignment of logical devices to physical devices.  DEVICE) 1778 SB
225 2002 1621 (    can also display the names and attributes of physical devices supported on your) 1621 SB
225 2061 1754 (    system.  If your system does not support the DEVTBL entry point, then the logical to) 1754 SB
225 2120 1061 (    physical device assignments are fixed by the BIOS.) 1061 SB
225 2239 1692 (      In general, BDOS serial I/O functions read and write an individual ASCII charac-) 1692 SB
225 2298 1673 (    ter, or character string to and from these devices, or test the device's ready status.) 1673 SB
225 2357 1694 (    For these BDOS functions, a string of characters is defined as zero to N characters) 1694 SB
225 2416 1684 (    terminated by a delimiter.  A block of characters is defined as zero to N characters) 1684 SB
225 2475 1701 (    where N is specified by a word count field.  The maximum value of N in both cases) 1701 SB
225 2535 1645 (    is limited only by available memory.  The following list summarizes BDOS serial) 1645 SB
225 2594 467 (    device I/O functions.) 467 SB
1166 2830 67 (2-2) 67 SB
