225 227 1700 (       The basic I/O functions also monitor the console to stop and start console output) 1700 SB
225 286 1676 (     scroll at the user's request.  To provide this support, the console output functions) 1676 SB
225 345 1699 (     make internal status checks for an input character before writing a character to the) 1699 SB
225 405 1709 (     output device.  The console input and console status functions also check the input) 1709 SB
225 464 1638 (     character.  If the user types a CTRL-S, these functions make an additional Blos) 1638 SB
225 523 1771 (     console input call.  This input call suspends execution until a character is typed.  If the) 1771 SB

