225 582 1663 (     typed character is not a CTRL-Q, an additional BIOS console input call is made.) 1663 SB
225 641 1498 (     Execution and console scrolling resume when the user types a CTRL-Q.) 1498 SB
225 760 1726 (       When the BDOS is suspended because of a typed CTRL-S, it scans input for three) 1726 SB
225 819 1663 (     special characters: CTRL-Q, CTRL-C, and CTRL-P.  If the user types any other) 1663 SB
225 878 1715 (     character, the BDOS echoes a bell character, CTRL-G, to the console, discards the) 1715 SB
225 937 1651 (     input character, and continues the scan.  If the user types a CTRL-C, the BDOS) 1651 SB
225 996 1637 (     executes a warm start which terminates the calling program.  If the user types a) 1637 SB
225 1055 1777 (     CTRL-P, the BDOS toggles the printer echo switch.  The printer echo switch controls) 1777 SB
225 1115 1739 (     whether console output is automatically echoed to the list device, LST:.  The BDOS) 1739 SB
225 1174 1628 (     signals when it turns on printer echo by sending a bell character to the console.) 1628 SB
225 1292 1701 (       All basic console I/O functions discard any CTRL-Q or CTRL-P character that is) 1701 SB
225 1351 1747 (     not preceded by a CTRL-S character.  Thus, BDOS function 1 cannot read a CTRL-) 1747 SB
225 1410 1756 (     S, CTRL-Q, or CTRL-P character.  Furthermore, these characters are invisible to the) 1756 SB
225 1470 533 (     console status function.) 533 SB
225 1588 1683 (       The second category of console I/O is direct console I/O.  BDOS function 6 can) 1683 SB
225 1647 1721 (     proveide direct console   I/O in situations where unadorned console I/O is required.) 1721 SB
225 1706 1769 (     Function 6 actually consists of several sub-functions that support direct console input,) 1769 SB
225 1765 1714 (     output, and status checks.   The BDOS does not filter out special characters during) 1714 SB
225 1825 1671 (     direct console I/O.  The direct output sub-function does not expand tabs, and the) 1671 SB
225 1884 1486 (     direct input sub-function does not echo typed characters to the console.) 1486 SB
225 2002 1725 (       The third category of console I/O accepts edited input from the console.  The only) 1725 SB
225 2061 1726 (     function in this category, Function 10, Read Buffer Input, reads an input line from a) 1726 SB
225 2120 1752 (     buffer and recognizes certain control characters that edit the input.  As an option, the) 1752 SB
225 2180 1196 (     line to be edited can be initialized by the calling program.) 1196 SB
225 2298 1689 (       In the nonbanked version of CP/M 3, editing within the buffer is restricted to the) 1689 SB
225 2357 1726 (     last character on the line.  That. is, to edit a character embedded in the line, the user) 1726 SB
225 2416 1726 (     must delete all characters that follow the erroneous character, correct the error, and) 1726 SB
225 2475 1619 (     then retype the remainder of the line.  The banked version of CP/M 3 supports) 1619 SB
225 2535 1747 (     complete line editing in which characters can be deleted and inserted anywhere in the) 1747 SB
225 2594 1637 (     line.  In addition', the banked version can also recall the previously entered line.) 1637 SB
1166 2830 67 (2-4) 67 SB
