0 0 0 fC
225 227 1630 (    bit 3 : This bit disables all CTRL-C intercept action in the BDOS.  This mode is) 1630 SB
225 286 1353 (            useful for programs that must control their own termination.) 1353 SB
225 405 1696 (    bits 8 and 9 : The BDOS does not use these bits, but reserves them for the CP/M 3) 1696 SB
225 464 1587 (            GET RSX that performs console input redirection from a file.  With one) 1587 SB
225 523 1623 (            exception, these bits determine how the GET RSX responds to a program) 1623 SB
225 582 1452 (            console status request \(Function 6, Function 11, or direct BIOS\).) 1452 SB
225 700 935 (            bit 8 =  0, bit 9 = 0  - conditional status) 935 SB
225 760 805 (            bit 8 =  0, bit 9 = 1  - false status) 805 SB
225 819 794 (            bit 8 =  1, bit 9 = 0  - true status) 794 SB
225 878 1102 (            bit 8 =  1, bit 9 = 1 - do not perform redirection) 1102 SB
225 996 1687 (      In conditional status mode, GET responds false to all status requests except for a) 1687 SB
225 1055 1654 (    status call preceded immediately by another status call.  On the second call, GET) 1654 SB
225 1115 1597 (    responds with a true result.  Thus, a program that spins on status to wait for a) 1597 SB
225 1174 1610 (    character is signaled that a character is ready on the second call.  In addition, a) 1610 SB
225 1233 1662 (    program that makes status calls periodically to see if the user wants to stop is not) 1662 SB
225 1292 226 (    signaled.) 226 SB
225 1410 1699 (       When  a transient program begins execution, the Console Mode bits are normally) 1699 SB
225 1470 1727 (    set to zero.  However,, the CP/M 3 utility GENCOM can attach an RSX header to a) 1727 SB
225 1529 1674 (    COM file so that when it is loaded, the console mode bits are set differently.  This) 1674 SB
225 1588 1658 (    feature allows you to modify a program's console I/O behavior without having to) 1658 SB
225 1647 460 (    change the program.) 460 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c34a font
225 1765 514 (    2.2.2 Other Serial I/O) 514 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 1884 1711 (      The BDOS supports single character output functions for the logical devices LST:) 1711 SB
225 1943 1658 (    and AUXOUT:, an input function for AUXIN:, and status functions for AUXIN:) 1658 SB
225 2002 1638 (    and AUXOUT:.  A block output function is also supported for the LST: device.) 1638 SB
225 2061 1725 (    Unlike the console I/O functions, the BDOS does not intercept control characters or) 1725 SB
225 2120 1632 (    expand tabs for these functions.  Note that AUXIN: and AUXOUT: replace the) 1632 SB
225 2180 1460 (    READER and PUNCH devices supported by earlier versions of CP/M.) 1460 SB
