SS
0 0 25 25 798 1100 300 SM
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
0 0 0 fC
225 227 1623 (     BDOS directory functions operate on existing file entries in a drive's directory.) 1623 SB
225 286 1705 (    This category includes functions to search for one or more files, delete one or more) 1705 SB
225 345 1707 (    files, truncate a file, rename a file, set file attributes, assign a password to a file, and) 1707 SB
225 405 1722 (    compute the size of a file.  The search and delete functions are the only BDOS func-) 1722 SB
225 464 1749 (    tions that support ambiguous file references.  All other directory and fi e related func-) 1749 SB
225 523 781 (    tions require a specific file reference.) 781 SB
225 641 1670 (     The BDOS drive-related category includes functions that select the default drive,) 1670 SB
225 700 1712 (    compute a drive's free space, interrogate drive status, and assign a directory label to) 1712 SB
225 760 1718 (    a drive.  A drive's directory label controls whether or not CP/M 3 enforces file pass-) 1718 SB
225 819 1669 (    word protection, or stamps files with the date and time.  Note that the nonbanked) 1669 SB
225 878 1076 (    version of CP/M 3 does not support file passwords.) 1076 SB
225 996 1638 (     The miscellaneous category includes functions to set the current DMA address,) 1638 SB
225 1055 1597 (    access and update the current user number, chain to a new program, and flush) 1597 SB
225 1115 1722 (    internal blocking/deblocking buffers.  Also included are functions that set the BDOS) 1722 SB
225 1174 1738 (    multi-sector count, and the BDOS error mode.  The BDOS multi-sector count deter-) 1738 SB
225 1233 1633 (    mines the number of 128-byte records to be processed by BDOS read and write) 1633 SB
225 1292 1695 (    functions.  It can range from 1 to 128.  The BDOS error mode determines how the) 1695 SB
225 1351 1061 (    BDOS file system handles certain classes of errors.) 1061 SB
225 1470 1759 (      Also included in the miscellaneous category are functions that call the BIOS directly,) 1759 SB
225 1529 1710 (    set a program return code, and parse filenames.  If the LOADER RSX is resident in) 1710 SB
225 1588 1730 (    memory, programs can also make a BDOS function call to load an overlay.  Another) 1730 SB
225 1647 1607 (    miscellaneous function accesses system variables in the System Control Block.) 1607 SB
