225 227 1737 (    The drive specifier field specifies the drive where the file is located. The filename and) 1737 SB
225 286 1631 (    type fields identify the file.  The password field specifies the password if a file is) 1631 SB
225 345 456 (    password protected.) 456 SB
225 464 1713 (      -ne drive, type, and password fields are optional, and the delimiters :.; are required) 1713 SB
225 523 1767 (    only when specifying their associated field.  The drive specifier can be assigned a letter) 1767 SB
225 582 1660 (    from A to P where the actual drive letters supported on a given system are deter-) 1660 SB
225 641 1760 (    mined by the BIOS implementation.  When the drive letter is not specified, the current) 1760 SB
225 700 540 (    default drive is assumed.) 540 SB
225 819 1664 (      The filename and password fields can contain one to eight non-delimiter charac-) 1664 SB
225 878 1694 (    ters.  The filetype field can contain one to three non-delimiter characters.  All three) 1694 SB
225 937 1703 (    fields are padded with blanks, if necessary.  Omitting the optional type or password) 1703 SB
225 996 969 (    fields implies a field specification of all blanks.) 969 SB
225 1115 1648 (      The CCP calls BDOS Function 152, Parse Filename, to parse file specifications) 1648 SB
225 1174 1664 (    from a command line.  Function 152 recognizes certain ASCII characters as valid) 1664 SB
225 1233 1728 (    delimiters when it parses a file from a command line.  The valid delimiters are shown) 1728 SB
225 1292 305 (    in Table 2-1.) 305 SB
