225 405 1820 (              Avoid using parentheses and the backslash character, \\, in the filename and filetype) 1820 SB
225 464 1790 (            fields because they are commonly used delimiters.  Use asterisk and question mark) 1790 SB
225 523 1799 (            characters, * and ?, only to make an ambiguous file reference.  When Function 152) 1799 SB
225 582 1815 (            encounters an * in a filename or filetype field, it pads the remainder of the field with) 1815 SB
225 641 1752 (            question marks.  For example, a filename of X*.* is parsed to X???????.???. The) 1752 SB
225 700 1840 (            BDOS search and delete functions treat a ? in the filename and type fields as follows:) 1840 SB
225 760 1821 (            A ? in any position matches the corresponding field of any directory entry belonging) 1821 SB
225 819 1795 (            to the current user number.  Thus, a search operation for X???????.??? finds all the) 1795 SB
225 878 1734 (            current user files on the directory beginning in X. Most other file related BDOS) 1734 SB
225 937 1618 (            functions treat the presence of a ? in the filename or type field as an error.) 1618 SB
225 1055 1740 (              It is not mandatory to follow the file naming conventions of CP/M 3 when you) 1740 SB
225 1115 1871 (            create or rename a file with BDOS functions.  However, the conventions must be used) 1871 SB
225 1174 1864 (            if the file is to be accessed from a command line.  For example, the CCP cannot locate) 1864 SB
225 1233 1744 (            a command file in the directory if its filename or type field contains a lower-case) 1744 SB
225 1292 272 (            letter.) 272 SB
225 1410 1793 (              As a general rule, the filetype field names the generic category of a particular file,) 1793 SB
225 1470 1813 (            while the filename distinguishes individual files in each category.  Although they are) 1813 SB
225 1529 1862 (            generally arbitrary, the following list of filetypes names some of the generic categories) 1862 SB
225 1588 697 (            that have  been established.) 697 SB
225 1706 406 (                 ASM      ) 406 SB
