225 1055 1780 (            For BDOS directory functions, the calling program must initialize bytes 0 through) 1780 SB
225 1115 1762 (          11 of the FCB before issuing the function call.  The Set Directory Label and Write) 1762 SB
225 1174 1864 (          File XFCB functions also require the calling program to initialize byte 12.  The Rename) 1864 SB
225 1233 1814 (          File function requires the calling program to place the new filename and type in bytes) 1814 SB
225 1292 425 (          17 through 27.) 425 SB
225 1410 1775 (            BDOS open or make function calls require the calling program to intialize bytes 0) 1775 SB
225 1470 1743 (          through 12 of the FCB before making the call.  Usually, byte 12 is set to zero.  In) 1743 SB
225 1529 1673 (                    if the file is to be processed from the beginning using sequential read or) 1673 SB
225 1588 342 (          addition, 1) 342 SB
225 1647 1006 (          write functions, byte 32, cr, must be zeroed.) 1006 SB
225 1765 1772 (           After an FCB is activated by an open or make operation, a program does not have) 1772 SB
225 1825 1764 (          to modify the FCB to perform sequential read or write operations.  In fact, bytes 0) 1764 SB
225 1884 1707 (          through 31 of an activated FCB should not be modified.  However, random I/O) 1707 SB
225 1943 1748 (          functions require that a program set bytes 33 through 35 to the requested random) 1748 SB
225 2002 1087 (          record number prior to making the function call.) 1087 SB
225 2120 1734 (           File directory entries maintained in the directory area of each disk have the same) 1734 SB
225 2180 1822 (          format as FCBS, excluding bytes 32 through 35, except for byte 0 which contains the) 1822 SB
225 2239 1771 (          file's user number.  Both the Open File and Make File functions bring these entries,) 1771 SB
225 2298 1805 (          excluding byte 0, into memory in the FCB specified by the calling program.  All read) 1805 SB
225 2357 1630 (          and write operations on a file must specify an FCB activated in this manner.) 1630 SB
