225 227 1733 (      The BDOS updates the memory copy of the FCB during file processing to maintain) 1733 SB
225 286 1711 (    the current position within the file.  During file write operations, the BDOS updates) 1711 SB
225 345 1681 (    the memory copy of the FCB to record the allocation of data to the file, and at the) 1681 SB
225 405 1728 (    termination of file processing, the Close File function permanently records this infor-) 1728 SB
225 464 1696 (    mation on disk.  Note that data allocated to a file during file write operations is not) 1696 SB
225 523 1740 (    completely recorded in the directory until the calling program issues a Close File call.) 1740 SB
225 582 1714 (    Therefore,, a program that creates or modifies files must close the files at the end of) 1714 SB
225 641 1095 (    any write processing.  Otherwise, data might be lost.) 1095 SB
225 760 1689 (      The BDOS Search and Delete functions support multiple or ambiguous file refer-) 1689 SB
225 819 1692 (    ences.  In general, a question mark in the filename, filetype, or extent field matches) 1692 SB
225 878 1728 (    any value in the corresponding positions of directory FCBs during a directory search) 1728 SB
225 937 1700 (    operation.  The BDOS search functions also recognize a question mark in the drive) 1700 SB
225 996 1706 (    code field, and if specified, they return all directory entries on the disk regardless of) 1706 SB
225 1055 1691 (    user number, including empty entries.  A directory FCB that begins with E5H is an) 1691 SB
225 1115 493 (    empty directory entry.) 493 SB
