251 1233 451 (  2.3.4 File Attributes) 451 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 1352 1617 (      The high-order bits of the FCB filename, fl',...,f8', and filetype, tl',t2',t3', fields) 1617 SB
225 1411 1718 (    are called attribute bits.  Attributes bits are 1 bit Boolean fields where 1 indicates on) 1718 SB
225 1471 1666 (    or true, and 0 indicates off or false.  Attribute bits indicate two kinds of attributes) 1666 SB
225 1530 1238 (    within the file system: file attributes and interface attributes.) 1238 SB
225 1648 1681 (      The file attribute bits, fl ...... f4' and tl',t2',t3', can indicate that a file has a defined) 1681 SB
225 1707 1758 (    file attribute.  These bits are recorded in a file's directory FCBS.  File attributes can be) 1758 SB
225 1766 1703 (    set or reset only by the BDOS Set File Attributes function.  When the BDOS Make) 1703 SB
225 1826 1635 (    File function creates a file, it initializes all file attributes to zero.  A program can) 1635 SB
225 1885 1728 (    interrogate file attributes in an FCB activated by the BDOS Open File function, or in) 1728 SB
225 1944 1783 (    directory FCBs returned by the BDOS Search For First and Search For Next functions.) 1783 SB
225 2062 1739 (    Note: the BDOS file system ignores file attribute bits when it attempts to locate a file) 1739 SB
225 2121 367 (    in the directory.) 367 SB
225 2240 1376 (       The file system defines the file attribute bits, tl',t2',t3', as follows:) 1376 SB
225 2358 1630 (    tl': Read-Only attribute - The file system prevents write operations to a file with) 1630 SB
225 2417 667 (           the read-only attribute set.) 667 SB
