225 286 1693 (       t2':  System attribute - This attribute, if set, identifies the file as a CP/M 3 system) 1693 SB
225 345 1696 (             file.  System files are not usually displayed by the CP/M 3 DIR command.  In) 1696 SB
225 405 1743 (             addition, user-zero system files can be accessed on a read-only basis from other) 1743 SB
225 464 446 (             user numbers.) 446 SB
225 582 1746 (       t3':  Archive attribute - This attribute is designed for user written archive programs.) 1746 SB
225 641 1670 (             When an archive program copies a file to backup storage, it sets the archive) 1670 SB
225 700 1688 (              attribute of the copied files.  The file system automatically resets the archive) 1688 SB
225 760 1758 (             attribute of a directory FCB that has been issued a write command.  The archive) 1758 SB
225 819 1755 (             program can test this attribute in each of the file's directory FCBs via the BDOS) 1755 SB
225 878 1734 (             Search and Search Next functions.  If all directory FCBs have the archive attri-) 1734 SB
225 937 1617 (             bute set, it indicates that the file has not been modified since the previous) 1617 SB
225 996 1428 (             archives Note that the CP/M 3 PIP utility supports file archival.) 1428 SB
225 1115 1341 (       Attributes fl' through f4' are available for definition by the user.) 1341 SB
225 1233 1724 (         The interface attributes are indicated by bits f5' through f8' and cannot be used as) 1724 SB
225 1292 1713 (       file attributes.  Interface attributes f5' and f6' can request options for BDOS Make) 1713 SB
225 1351 1839 (       File, Close File, Delete File, and Set File Attributes functions.  Table 2-3 defines options) 1839 SB
225 1410 1451 (       indicated by the f5' and f6' interface attribute bits for these functions.) 1451 SB
225 1529 1167 (                               Table 2-3.  BDOS Interface Attributes) 1167 SB
225 1588 1421 (                       BDOS Function                 Interface Attribute Definition) 1421 SB
225 1706 1198 (                    16. Close File                   f5'    1   Partial Close) 1198 SB
225 1825 1326 (                    19. Delete File                  f5'     1   Delete file XFCBs) 1326 SB
225 1884 930 (                                                                 only) 930 SB
225 2002 1364 (                    22. Make File                    f6' = 1    Assign password to) 1364 SB
225 2061 893 (                                                                file) 893 SB
225 2180 1369 (                    30. Set File Attributes          f6' = 1    Set file byte count) 1369 SB
225 2357 1711 (       Section 3 discusses each interface attribute in detail in the definitions of the above) 1711 SB
225 2416 1672 (       functions.  Attributes f5' and f6' are always reset when control is returned to the) 1672 SB
225 2475 1722 (       calling program.  Interface attributes f7' and f8' are reserved for internal use by the) 1722 SB
225 2535 459 (       BDOS file system.) 459 SB
