225 227 1707 (       An XFCB can be created only on a drive that has a directory label, and only if the) 1707 SB
225 286 1731 (     directory label has activated password protection.  For drives in this state, an XFCB) 1731 SB
225 345 1714 (     can be created for a file in two ways: by the BDOS Make function or by the BDOS) 1714 SB
225 405 1754 (     Write File XFCB function.  The BDOS Make function creates an XFCB if the calling) 1754 SB
225 464 1724 (     program requests that a password be assigned to the created file.  The BDOS Write) 1724 SB
225 523 1754 (     File XFCB function can be used to assign a password to an existing file.  Note that in) 1754 SB
225 582 1705 (     the directory, an XFCB is identified by a drive byte value, byte 0 in the FCB, equal) 1705 SB
225 641 938 (     to 16 + N, where N equals the user number.) 938 SB
225 760 1741 (       For its drive, the directory label specifies if file password support is to be activated,) 1741 SB
225 819 1716 (     and if date and time stamping for files is to be performed.  The format of the Direc-) 1716 SB
225 878 441 (     tory Label follows.) 441 SB
