225 1470 545 (         2.3.7 File Passwords) 545 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 1588 1710 (           Only the banked version of CP/M 3 supports file passwords.  In the nonbanked) 1710 SB
225 1647 1801 (         version, all BDOS functions with password related options operate the same way the) 1801 SB
225 1706 1190 (         banked version does when passwords are not enabled.) 1190 SB
225 1825 1755 (           Files can be assigned passwords in two ways: by the Make File function or by the) 1755 SB
225 1884 1764 (         Write File XFCB function.  A file's password can also be changed by the Write File) 1764 SB
225 1943 1136 (         XFCB function if the original password is supplied.) 1136 SB
225 2061 1805 (           Password protection is provided in one of three modes.  Table 2-4 shows the differ-) 1805 SB
225 2120 1771 (         ence in access level allowed to BDOS functions when the password is not supplied.) 1771 SB
1154 2830 92 (2-21) 92 SB
