225 227 1129 (                          Table 2-4.  Password Protection Modes) 1129 SB
225 286 1379 (                  Password           Access level allowed wben the Password) 1379 SB
225 345 885 (                  Mode                  is not supplied.) 885 SB
225 464 1011 (                  1. Read            The file cannot be read.) 1011 SB
225 582 1298 (                  2. Write           The file can be read, but not modified.) 1298 SB
225 700 1190 (                  3. Delete          The file can be modified, but not) 1190 SB
225 760 702 (                                          deleted.) 702 SB
225 937 1727 (    If a file is password protected in Read mode, the password must be supplied to open) 1727 SB
225 996 1702 (    the file.  A file protected in Write mode cannot be written to without the password.) 1702 SB
225 1055 1623 (    A file protected in Delete mode allows read and write access, but the user must) 1623 SB
225 1115 1637 (        'fy the password to delete the file, rename the file, or to modify the file's attri-) 1637 SB
225 1174 152 (    speci) 152 SB
225 1233 1686 (    butes.  Thus, password protection in mode 1 implies mode 2 and 3 protection, and) 1686 SB
225 1292 1677 (    mode 2 protection implies mode 3 protection.  All three modes require the user to) 1677 SB
225 1351 1778 (    specify the password to delete the file, rename the file, or to modify the file's attributes.) 1778 SB
225 1470 1642 (      If the correct password is supplied, or if password protection is disabled by the) 1642 SB
225 1529 1682 (    Directory Label, then access to the BDOS functions is the same as for a file that is) 1682 SB
225 1588 1737 (    not password protected.  In addition, the Search For First and Search For Next func-) 1737 SB
225 1647 839 (    tions are not affected by file passwords.) 839 SB
225 1765 1207 (    Table 2-5 lists the BDOS functions that test for password.) 1207 SB
