225 227 1741 (         File passwords are eight bytes in length.  They are maintained in the XFCB Direc-) 1741 SB
225 286 1767 (        tory Label in encrypted form.  To make a BDOS function call for a file that requires) 1767 SB
225 345 1783 (        a password, a program must place the password in the first eight bytes of the current) 1783 SB
225 405 1766 (        DMA, or specify it with the BDOS function, Set Default Password, prior to making) 1766 SB
225 464 435 (        the function call.) 435 SB
225 523 1772 (        Note: the BDOS keeps an assigned default password value until it is replaced with a) 1772 SB
225 582 498 (        new assigned value.) 498 SB
