225 760 1720 (         The CP/M 3 File System uses a special type of directory entry called an SFCB to) 1720 SB
225 819 1763 (        record date and time stamps for files.  When a directory has been initialized for date) 1763 SB
225 878 1831 (        and time stamping, SFCBs reside in every fourth position of the directory.  Each SFCB) 1831 SB
225 937 1768 (        maintains the date and time stamps for the previous three directory entries as shown) 1768 SB
225 996 374 (        in Figure 2-3.) 374 SB
