225 1936 1206 (                             Figure 2-3.  Directory Record with SFCB) 1206 SB
225 2054 1824 (        This figure shows a directory record that contains an SFCB.  Directory records consist) 1824 SB
225 2113 1781 (        of four directory entries, each 32 bytes long.  SFCBs always occupy the last position) 1781 SB
225 2172 527 (        of a directory record.) 527 SB
225 2350 1729 (          The SFCB directory item contains five fields.  The first field is one byte long and) 1729 SB
225 2409 1730 (        contains the value 21H.  This value identifies the SFCB in the directory.  The next) 1730 SB
225 2468 1712 (        three fields, the SFCB subfields, contain the date and time stamps for their corre-) 1712 SB
225 2527 1816 (        sponding FCB entries in the directory record.  These fields are 10 bytes long.  The last) 1816 SB
225 2586 1726 (        byte of the SFCB is reserved for system use.  The format of the SFCB subfields is) 1726 SB
225 2646 499 (        shown in Table 2-6.) 499 SB
1154 2823 92 (2-23) 92 SB
