225 227 1093 (                              Table 2-6.  SFCB Subfields Format) 1093 SB
225 286 1191 (                  Offset in Bytes  I          SFCB Subfield Contents) 1191 SB
225 405 1381 (                    0 - 3           Create or Access Date and Time Stamp field) 1381 SB
225 464 1187 (                    4 - 7           Update Date and Time Stamp field) 1187 SB
225 523 907 (                      8              Password mode field) 907 SB
225 582 677 (                      9              Reserved) 677 SB
225 760 1728 (       An SFCB subfield contains   valid information only if its corresponding FCB in the) 1728 SB
225 819 1721 (    directory record is an extent  zero FCB. This FCB is a file's first directory entry. For) 1721 SB
225 878 1733 (    password protected files, the  SFCB subfield also contains the password mode of the) 1733 SB
225 937 1784 (    file.  This field is zero for files that are not password protected.  The BDOS Search and) 1784 SB
225 996 1656 (    Search Next functions can be used to access SFCBs directly.  In addition, BDOS) 1656 SB
225 1055 1622 (    Function 102 can return the file date and time stamps and password mode for a) 1622 SB
225 1115 1692 (    specified file.  Refer to Section 3, function 102, for a description of the format of a) 1692 SB
225 1174 562 (    date and time stamp field.) 562 SB
225 1292 1695 (       CP/M 3 supports three types of file stamping: create, access, and update.  Create) 1695 SB
225 1351 1728 (    stamps record when the file was created, access stamps record when the file was last) 1728 SB
225 1410 1665 (    opened, and update stamps record the last time the file was modified.  Create and) 1665 SB
225 1470 1777 (    access stamps share the same field.  As a result, file access stamps overwrite any create) 1777 SB
225 1529 202 (    stamps.) 202 SB
225 1647 1705 (      The CP/M 3 utility, INITDIR, initializes a directory for date and time stamping by) 1705 SB
225 1706 1688 (    placing SFCBs in every fourth directory entry.  Date and time stamping is not sup-) 1688 SB
225 1765 1728 (    ported on disks that have not been initialized in this manner.  For initialized disks the) 1728 SB
225 1825 1695 (    disks' Directory Label determines the type of date and time stamping supported for) 1695 SB
225 1884 1720 (    files on the drive.  If a disk does not have a Directory Label, or if it is Read-Only, or) 1720 SB
225 1943 1698 (    if the disk's Directory Label does not specify date and time stamping, then date and) 1698 SB
225 2002 1697 (    time stamping for files is not performed.  Note that the Directory Label is also time) 1697 SB
225 2061 1679 (    stamped, but these stamps are not made in an SFCB.  Time stamp fields in the last) 1679 SB
225 2120 1619 (    eight bytes of the Directory Label record when it was created and last updated.) 1619 SB
225 2180 1146 (    Access stamping for Directory Labels is not supported.) 1146 SB
