225 227 1752 (              The BDOS file system uses the CP/M 3 system date and time when it records a) 1752 SB
225 286 1855 (              date and time stamp.  This value is maintained in a field in the System Control Block) 1855 SB
225 345 1888 (              \(SCB\).  On CP/M 3 systems that support a hardware clock, the BIOS module directly) 1888 SB
225 405 1870 (              updates the SCB system date and time field.  Otherwise, date and time stamps record) 1870 SB
225 464 1858 (              the last initialized value for the system date and time.  The CP/M 3 DATE utility can) 1858 SB
225 523 970 (              be used to set the system date and time.) 970 SB
