225 227 1696 (         The BDOS Error Mode, which can exist in three states, determines how the file) 1696 SB
225 286 1791 (        system handles physical and extended errors.  In the default state, the BDOS displays) 1791 SB
225 345 1694 (        the error message, and terminates the calling program, method 2. In return error) 1694 SB
225 405 1738 (        mode, the BDOS returns control to the calling program with the error identified in) 1738 SB
225 464 1678 (        registers A, H, and L, method 1. In return and display mode, the BDOS returns) 1678 SB
225 523 1758 (        control to the calling program with the error identified in registers A, H, and L, and) 1758 SB
225 582 1738 (        also displays the error message at the console, method 3. While both return modes) 1738 SB
225 641 1687 (        protect a program from termination because of a physical or extended error, the) 1687 SB
225 700 1705 (        return and display mode also allows the calling program to take advantage of the) 1705 SB
225 760 1731 (        built-in error reporting of the BDOS file system.  Physical and extended errors are) 1731 SB
225 819 1073 (        displayed on the console in the following format:) 1073 SB
225 937 802 (            CP/M Error on d: error message) 802 SB
225 996 949 (            BDOS function = nn File = filename.typ) 949 SB
225 1115 1775 (        where d identifies the drive selected when the error condition is detected; error mes-) 1775 SB
225 1174 1801 (         sage identifies the error; nn is the BDOS function number, and filename.typ identifies) 1801 SB
225 1233 1718 (        the file specified by the BDOS function.  If the BDOS function did not involve an) 1718 SB
225 1292 1716 (        FCB, the file information is omitted.  Note that the second line of the above error) 1716 SB
225 1351 1802 (        message is displayed only in the banked version of CP/M 3 if expanded error message) 1802 SB
225 1410 1760 (        reporting is requested in GENCPM.  It is not displayed in the nonbanked version of) 1760 SB
225 1470 274 (        CP/M 3.) 274 SB
225 1588 1573 (         The BDOS physical errors are identified by the following error messages:) 1573 SB
225 1706 367 (            o Disk I/O) 367 SB
225 1765 455 (            o Invalid Drive) 455 SB
225 1825 495 (            o Read-Only File) 495 SB
225 1884 514 (            o Read-Only Disk) 514 SB
225 2002 1734 (        The Disk I/O error results from an error condition returned to the BDOS from the) 1734 SB
225 2061 1824 (        BIOS module.  The file system makes BIOS read and write calls to execute file-related) 1824 SB
225 2120 1733 (        BDOS calls.  If the BIOS read or write routine detects an error, it returns an error) 1733 SB
225 2180 914 (        code to the BDOS resulting in this error.) 914 SB
225 2298 1758 (          The Invalid Drive error also results from an error condition returned to the BDOS) 1758 SB
225 2357 1806 (        from the BIOS module.  The BDOS makes a BIOS Select Disk call prior to accessing) 1806 SB
225 2416 1721 (        a drive to perform a requested BDOS function.  If the BIOS does not support the) 1721 SB
225 2475 1641 (        selected disk, the BDOS returns an error code resulting in this error message.) 1641 SB
1154 2830 92 (2-29) 92 SB
