225 227 1642 (     The Read-Only File error is returned when a program attempts to write to a file) 1642 SB
225 286 1648 (   that is marked with the Read-Only attribute.  It is also returned to a program that) 1648 SB
225 345 1581 (   attempts to write to a system file opened under user zero from a nonzero user) 1581 SB
225 405 1651 (   number.  In addition, this error is returned when a program attempts to write to a) 1651 SB
225 464 1650 (   file password protected in Write mode if the program does not supply the correct) 1650 SB
225 523 241 (   password.) 241 SB
225 641 1645 (     The Read-Only Disk error is returned when a program writes to a disk that is in) 1645 SB
225 700 1713 (   read-only status.  A drive can be placed in read-only status explicitly with the BDOS) 1713 SB
225 760 603 (   Write Protect Disk function.) 603 SB
225 878 1541 (     The BDOS extended errors are identified by the following error messages:) 1541 SB
225 996 456 (        o Password Error) 456 SB
225 1055 349 (        o File Exists) 349 SB
225 1115 404 (        o ? in Filename) 404 SB
225 1233 1607 (     The File Password error is returned when the file password is not supplied, or) 1607 SB
225 1292 1663 (   when it is incorrect.  This error is reported only by the banked version of CP/M 3.) 1663 SB
225 1410 1648 (     The File Exists error is returned by the BDOS Make File and Rename File func-) 1648 SB
225 1470 1582 (   tions when the BDOS detects a conflict such as a duplicate filename and type.) 1582 SB
225 1588 1671 (     The ? in Filename error is returned when the BDOS detects a ? in the filename or) 1671 SB
225 1647 1674 (   type field of the passed FCB for the BDOS Rename File, Set File Attributes, Open) 1674 SB
225 1706 919 (   File, Make File, and Truncate File functions.) 919 SB
225 1825 1702 (     The following paragraphs describe the error return code conventions of the BDOS) 1702 SB
225 1884 1690 (   file system functions.  Most BDOS file system functions fall into three categories in) 1690 SB
225 1943 1643 (   regard to return codes: they return an Error Code, a Directory Code, or an Error) 1643 SB
225 2002 1690 (   Flag.  The error conventions of CP/M 3 are designed to allow programs written for) 1690 SB
225 2061 1098 (   earlier versions of CP/M to run without modification.) 1098 SB
225 2180 1388 (     The following BDOS functions return an Error Code in register A.) 1388 SB
225 2298 502 (        20. Read Sequential) 502 SB
225 2357 512 (        21. Write Sequential) 512 SB
225 2416 462 (        33. Read Random) 462 SB
225 2475 472 (        34. Write Random) 472 SB
225 2535 706 (        40. Write Random w/Zero Fill) 706 SB
