225 1410 1678 (        For BDOS read or write functions, the file system also sets register H when the) 1678 SB
225 1470 1652 (        returned Error Code is a value other than zero or 255.  In this case, register H) 1652 SB
225 1529 1790 (        contains the number of 128-byte records successfully read or written before the error) 1790 SB
225 1588 1796 (        was encountered.  Note that register H can contain only a nonzero value if the calling) 1796 SB
225 1647 1770 (        program has set the BDOS Multi-Sector Count to a value other than one; otherwise) 1770 SB
225 1706 1768 (        register H is set to zero.  On successful functions, Error Code = 0, register H is also) 1768 SB
225 1765 1753 (        set to zero.  If the Error Code equals 255, register H contains a physical error code) 1753 SB
225 1825 443 (        \(see Table 2-11\).) 443 SB
