225 227 1763 (          The CCP initializes Page Zero prior to initiating a transient program.  The fields at) 1763 SB
225 286 1743 (        0050H and above are initialized from the command line invoking the transient pro-) 1743 SB
225 345 1735 (        gram.  The command line format was described in detail in Section 1.6.2. To sum-) 1735 SB
225 405 1036 (        marize, a command line usually takes the form:) 1036 SB
225 523 754 (             <command> <command tail>) 754 SB
225 641 225 (        where) 225 SB
225 760 935 (             <command>             = >    <file Spec>) 935 SB
225 878 1081 (             <command tail>        = >    \(no command tail\)) 1081 SB
225 937 455 (                                   ) 455 SB
825 937 348 (= >    <file Spec>) 348 SB
225 996 455 (                                   ) 455 SB
825 996 787 (= >    <file spec><delimiter><file spec>) 787 SB
225 1115 530 (             <file spec>           ) 530 SB
825 1115 783 (= >    {d:}filename{.type} {;password}) 783 SB
225 1233 1690 (        The CCP initializes the command drive field at 0050H to the drive index, A = 1,) 1690 SB
225 1292 1416 (        P = 16, of the drive from which the transient program was loaded.) 1416 SB
225 1410 1759 (          The default FCB at 005CH is defined if a command tail is entered.  Otherwise, the) 1759 SB
225 1470 1767 (        fields at 005CH, 0068H to 006BH are set to binary zeros, the fields from 005DH to) 1767 SB
225 1529 1747 (        0067H are set to blanks.  The fields at 0051H through 0053H are set if a password) 1747 SB
225 1588 1798 (        is specified for the first <file Spec> of the command tail.  If not, these fields are set to) 1798 SB
225 1647 204 (        zero.) 204 SB
225 1765 1690 (          The default FCB at 006CH is defined if a second <file spec> exists in the com-) 1690 SB
225 1825 1777 (        mand tail.  Otherwise, the fields at 006CH, 0078H to 007BH are set to binary zeros,) 1777 SB
225 1884 1692 (        the fields from 005DH to 0067H are set to blanks.  The fields at 0054H through) 1692 SB
225 1943 1752 (        0056H are set if a password is specified for the second <file spec> of the command) 1752 SB
225 2002 870 (        tail.  If not, these fields are set to zero.) 870 SB
225 2120 1738 (          Transient programs often use the default FCB at 005CH for file operations.  This) 1738 SB
225 2180 1692 (        FCB may even be used for random file access because the three bytes starting at) 1692 SB
225 2239 1763 (        007DH are available for this purpose.  However, a transient program must copy the) 1763 SB
225 2298 1760 (        contents of the default FCB at 006CH to another area before using the default FCB) 1760 SB
225 2357 1755 (        at 005CH, because an open operation for the default FCB at 005CH overwrites the) 1755 SB
225 2416 514 (        FCB data at 006CH.) 514 SB
