225 227 1696 (      The default DMA address for transient programs is 0080H.  The CCP also initial-) 1696 SB
225 286 1668 (    izes this area to contain the command tall of the command line.  The first position) 1668 SB
225 345 1673 (    contains the number of characters in the command line, followed by the command) 1673 SB
225 405 1648 (    line characters.  The character following the last command tail character is set to) 1648 SB
225 464 1689 (    binary zero.  The command line characters are preceded by a leading blank and are) 1689 SB
225 523 1725 (    translated to ASCII upper-case.  Because the 128-byte region beginning at 0080H is) 1725 SB
225 582 1686 (    the default DMAI, the BDOS file system moves 128-byte records to this area with) 1686 SB
225 641 1709 (    read operations and accesses 128-byte records from this area with write operations.) 1709 SB
225 700 1672 (    The transient program must extract the command tail information from this buffer) 1672 SB
225 760 1707 (    before performing file operations unless it explicitly changes the DMA address with) 1707 SB
225 819 829 (    the BDOS Set DMA Address function.) 829 SB
225 937 1691 (      The Page Zero fields of 0051H through OOS6H locate the password fields of the) 1691 SB
225 996 1757 (    first two file specifications in the command tail if they exist.  These fields are provided) 1757 SB
225 1055 1699 (    so that transient programs are not required to parse the command tail for password) 1699 SB
225 1115 1739 (    fields.  However, the transient program must save the password, or change the DMA) 1739 SB
225 1174 881 (    address before performing file operations.) 881 SB
225 1292 1654 (      The following example illustrates the initialization of the command line fields of) 1654 SB
225 1351 1525 (    Page Zero.  Assuming the following command line is typed at the console:) 1525 SB
225 1470 1549 (        D>A:PROGRAM B:FILE,TYPE ; PASS C ;FILE.TYPE ; PASSWORD) 1549 SB
225 1588 1698 (    A hexadecimal dump of 0050H to 0OA5H would show the Page Zero initialization) 1698 SB
225 1647 512 (    performed by the CCP.) 512 SB
225 1765 1806 (    005OH:  01 0D  00 04 9D  00 08 00  00  00 00 00 02 46 49  4C  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .FIL) 1806 SB
225 1825 1806 (    006OH:  45 20   20 20  20  54 59 50  00  00 00 00 03 46 49  4C E . . . . TYP . . . . . FIL) 1806 SB
225 1884 1789 (    007OH:  45 20   20 20  20  54 59 50  00  00 00 00 00 00 00  00 E . . . . TYP . . . . . . . .) 1789 SB
225 1943 1788 (    0050H:   24 20   42 3A 46  49 4C 45  2E 54 59 50 3B 50 41 53 .  .   B:FILE.TYP;PAS) 1788 SB
225 2002 1788 (    009OH:  53 20  43 3A 46  49 4C 45  2E  54 59 50 3B 50 41 53  S    C:FILE.TYP;PAS) 1788 SB
225 2061 1519 (    OOAOH:  53 57  4F 52 44  00                                                   SWORD.) 1519 SB
