225 227 1206 (                        BDOS FUNCTION 1: CONSOLE INPUT) 1206 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 592 (                  Entry Parameters:) 592 SB
225 405 649 (                         Register C: 01H) 649 SB
225 523 561 (                  Returned Value:) 561 SB
525 582 590 ( Register A: ASCII Character) 590 SB
225 760 1601 (     The Console Input function reads the next character from the logical console,) 1601 SB
225 819 1734 (    CONIN:, to register A. Graphic characters, along with carriage return, line-feed, and) 1734 SB
225 878 1826 (    backspace, CTRL-H, are echoed to the console.  Tab characters, CTR-L-1, are expanded) 1826 SB
225 937 1766 (    in columns of 8 characters.  CTRL-S, CTRL-Q, and CTRL-P are normally intercepted) 1766 SB
225 996 1698 (    as described below.  All other non-graphic characters are returned in register A but) 1698 SB
225 1055 650 (    are not echoed to the console.) 650 SB
225 1174 1620 (      When the Console Mode is in the default state \(see Section 2.2.1\), Function 1) 1620 SB
225 1233 1739 (    intercepts the stop scroll, CTRL-S, start scroll, CTRL-Q, and start/stop printer echo,) 1739 SB
225 1292 1742 (    CTRL-P, characters.  Any characters that are typed following a CTRL-S and preced-) 1742 SB
225 1351 1694 (    ing a CTRL-Q are also intercepted.  However, if start/stop scroll has been disabled) 1694 SB
225 1410 1725 (    by the Console Mode, the CTRL-S, CTRL-Q, and CTRL-P characters are not inter-) 1725 SB
225 1470 1690 (    cepted.  Instead, they are returned in register A, but are not echoed to the console.) 1690 SB
225 1588 1686 (      If printer echo has been invoked, all characters that are echoed to the console are) 1686 SB
225 1647 705 (    also sent to the list device, LST:.) 705 SB
225 1765 1675 (      Function 1 does not return control to the calling program until a non-intercepted) 1675 SB
225 1825 1477 (    character is typed, thus suspending execution if a character is not ready.) 1477 SB
1166 2830 67 (3-2) 67 SB
