225 996 1742 (          CP/M 3 supports direct I/O to the logical console, CONIN:, for those specialized) 1742 SB
225 1055 1778 (       applications where unadorned console input and output is required.  Use Direct Con-) 1778 SB
225 1115 1671 (       sole I/O carefully because it bypasses all the normal control character functions.) 1671 SB
225 1174 1782 (       Programs that perform direct I/O through the BIOS under previous releases of CP/M) 1782 SB
225 1233 1751 (       should be changed to use direct I/O so that they can be fully supported under future) 1751 SB
225 1292 672 (       releases of MP/M and CP/M.) 672 SB
