225 878 1673 (            The Select Disk function designates the disk drive named in register E as the) 1673 SB
225 937 1803 (          default disk for subsequent BDOS file operations.  Register E is set to 0 for drive A,) 1803 SB
225 996 1816 (          1 for drive B, and so on through 15 for drive P in a full 16-drive system.  In addition,) 1816 SB
225 1055 1797 (          Function 14 logs in the designated drive if it is currently in the reset state.  Logging-) 1797 SB
225 1115 1806 (          in a drive activates the drive's directory until the next disk system reset or drive reset) 1806 SB
225 1174 332 (          operation.) 332 SB
225 1292 1796 (            FCBs that specify drive code zero \(dr = 00H\) automatically reference the currently) 1796 SB
225 1351 1733 (          selected default drive.  FCBs with drive code values between 1 and 16, however,) 1733 SB
225 1410 1596 (          gnore the selected default drive and directly reference drives A through P.) 1596 SB
225 1529 1785 (            Upon return, register A contains a zero if the select operation was successful.  If a) 1785 SB
225 1588 1833 (          physical error was encountered, the select function performs different actions depend-) 1833 SB
225 1647 1763 (          ing on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is in the) 1763 SB
225 1706 1733 (          'default mode, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console, and the) 1733 SB
225 1765 1761 (          calling program is terminated.  Otherwise, the select function returns to the calling) 1761 SB
225 1825 1703 (          program with register A set to OFFH and register H set to one of the following) 1703 SB
225 1884 542 (          physical error codes:) 542 SB
225 2002 577 (               01   Disk I/O Error) 577 SB
225 2061 533 (               04   Invalid drive) 533 SB
