225 878 1705 (      The Open File function activates the FCB for a file that exists in the disk directory) 1705 SB
225 937 1722 (    under the currently active user number or user zero.  The calling program passes the) 1722 SB
225 996 1709 (    address of the FCB in register pair DE, with byte 0 of the FCB specifying the drive,) 1709 SB
225 1055 1676 (    bytes 1 through 11 specifying the filename and filetype, and byte 12 specifying the) 1676 SB
225 1115 1183 (    extent.  Usually, byte 12 of the FCB is initialized to zero.) 1183 SB
225 1233 1604 (      If the file is password protected in Read mode, the correct password must be) 1604 SB
225 1292 1661 (    placed in the first eight bytes of the current DMA, or have been previously estab-) 1661 SB
225 1351 1700 (    lished as the default password \(see Function 106\).  If the current record field of the) 1700 SB
225 1410 1720 (    FCB, cr, is set to OFFH, Function 15 returns the byte count of the last record of the) 1720 SB
225 1470 1726 (    file in the cr field.  You can set the last record byte count for a file with Function 30,) 1726 SB
225 1529 1739 (    Set File Attributes.  Note that the current record field of the FCB, cr, must be zeroed) 1739 SB
225 1588 1677 (    by the calling program before beginning read or write operations if the file is to be) 1677 SB
225 1647 899 (    accessed sequentially from the first record.) 899 SB
225 1765 1673 (      If the current user is non-zero, and the file to be opened does not exist under the) 1673 SB
225 1825 1763 (    current user number, the open function searches user zero for the file.  If the file exists) 1763 SB
225 1884 1678 (    under user zero, and has the system attribute, t2', set, the file is opened under user) 1678 SB
225 1943 1716 (    zero.  Write operations are not supported for a file that is opened under user zero in) 1716 SB
225 2002 294 (    this manner.) 294 SB
