225 227 1156 (                           BDOS FUNCTION 16: CLOSE FILE) 1156 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 592 (                  Entry Parameters:) 592 SB
225 405 655 (                        Registers C: 10H) 655 SB
225 464 804 (                                  DE: FCB Address) 804 SB
225 582 561 (                  Returned Value:) 561 SB
225 641 880 (                        Registers A: Directory Code) 880 SB
225 700 1110 (                                       H: Physical or Extended Error) 1110 SB
225 878 1715 (     The Close File function performs the inverse of the Open File function.  The calling) 1715 SB
225 937 1747 (    program passes the address of an FCB in register pair DE.  The referenced FCB must) 1747 SB
225 996 1619 (    have been previously activated by a successful Open or Make function call \(see) 1619 SB
225 1055 1707 (    Functions 15 and 22\).  Interface attribute f5' specifies how the file is to be closed as) 1707 SB
225 1115 328 (    shown below:) 328 SB
225 1233 905 (        f5' = 0 - Permanent close \(default mode\)) 905 SB
225 1292 516 (        f5' = 1 - Partial close) 516 SB
225 1410 1747 (    A permanent close operation indicates that the program has completed file operations) 1747 SB
225 1470 1723 (    on the file.  A partial close operation updates the directory, but indicates that the file) 1723 SB
225 1529 776 (    is to be maintained in the open state.) 776 SB
225 1647 1700 (     If the referenced FCB contains new information because of write operations to the) 1700 SB
225 1706 1695 (    FCB, the close function permanently records the new information in the referenced) 1695 SB
225 1765 1710 (    disk directory.  Note that the FCB does not contain new information, and the direc-) 1710 SB
225 1825 1728 (    tory update step is bypassed if only read or update operations have been made to the) 1728 SB
225 1884 379 (    referenced FCB.) 379 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-22) 92 SB
225 92 861 (BDOS Function Calls                                 ) 861 SB
1605 92 570 (CP/M 3 Programmers Guide) 570 SB
