225 227 1671 (          Upon return, the close function returns a directory code in register A with the) 1671 SB
225 286 1811 (        value 00H if the close was successful,, or FFH, 255 Decimal, if the file was not found.) 1811 SB
225 345 1704 (        Register H is set to zero in both of these cases.  If a physical or extended error is) 1704 SB
225 405 1749 (        encountered, the close function performs different actions depending on the BDOS) 1749 SB
225 464 1700 (        error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is in the default mode, a) 1700 SB
225 523 1747 (        message identifying the error is displayed at the console, and the calling program is) 1747 SB
225 582 1800 (        terminated.  Otherwise, the close function returns to the calling program with register) 1800 SB
225 641 1658 (        A set to OFFH and register H set to one of the following physical error codes:) 1658 SB
225 760 542 (             01   Disk I/O error) 542 SB
225 819 553 (             02   Read/only disk) 553 SB
225 878 619 (             04   Invalid drive error) 619 SB
