225 227 1266 (                     BDOS FUNCTION 17: SEARCH FOR FIRST) 1266 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 592 (                  Entry Parameters:) 592 SB
225 405 655 (                        Registers C: 11H) 655 SB
225 464 843 (                                     DE: FCB Address) 843 SB
225 582 561 (                  Returned Value:) 561 SB
225 641 880 (                        Registers A: Directory Code) 880 SB
225 700 853 (                                       H: Physical Error) 853 SB
225 878 1765 (     The Search For First function scans the directory for a match with the FCB addressed) 1765 SB
225 937 1743 (   by register pair DE.  Two types of searches can be performed.  For standard searches,) 1743 SB
225 996 1710 (   the calling program initializes bytes 0 through 12 of the referenced FCB, with byte 0) 1710 SB
225 1055 1731 (   specifying the drive directory to be searched, bytes 1 through 11 specifying the file or) 1731 SB
225 1115 1695 (   files to be searched for,, and byte 12 specifying the extent.  Usually byte 12 is set to) 1695 SB
225 1174 1722 (   zero.  An ASCII question mark, 63 decimal, 3F hex, in any of the bytes 1 through 12) 1722 SB
225 1233 1736 (   matches all entries on the directory in the corresponding position.  This facility, called) 1736 SB
225 1292 1721 (   ambiguous reference, can be used to search for multiple files on the directory.  When) 1721 SB
225 1351 1659 (   called in the standard mode, the Search function scans for the first file entry in the) 1659 SB
225 1410 1664 (   specified directory that matches the FCB, and belongs to the current user number.) 1664 SB
225 1529 1675 (     The Search For First function also initializes the Search For Next function.  After) 1675 SB
225 1588 1738 (   the Search function has located the first directory entry matching the referenced FCB,) 1738 SB
225 1647 1706 (   the Search For Next function can be called repeatedly to locate all remaining match-) 1706 SB
225 1706 1715 (   ing entries.  In terms of execution sequence, however, the Search For Next call must) 1715 SB
225 1765 1652 (   either follow a Search For First or Search For Next call with no other intervening) 1652 SB
225 1825 707 (   BDOS disk-related function calls.) 707 SB
225 1943 1595 (     If byte 0 of the referenced FCB is set to a question mark, the Search function) 1595 SB
225 2002 1643 (   ignores the remainder of the referenced FCB, and locates the first directory entry) 1643 SB
225 2061 1688 (   residing on the current default drive.  All remaining directory entries can be located) 1688 SB
225 2120 1598 (   by making multiple Search For Next calls.  This type of search operation is not) 1598 SB
225 2180 1630 (   usually made by application programs, but it does provide complete flexibility to) 1630 SB
225 2239 1640 (   scan all current directory values.  Note that this type of search operation must be) 1640 SB
225 2298 1309 (   performed to access a drive's directory label \(see Section 2.3.6\).) 1309 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-24) 92 SB
225 92 861 (BDOS Function Calls                                 ) 861 SB
1605 92 570 (CP/M 3 Programmers Guide) 570 SB
