225 227 1727 (          Upon return, the Search function returns a Directory Code in register A with the) 1727 SB
225 286 1808 (        value 0 to 3 if the search is successful, or OFFH, 255 Decimal, if a matching directory) 1808 SB
225 345 1734 (        entry is not found.  Register H is set to zero in both of these cases.  For successful) 1734 SB
225 405 1689 (        searches, the current DMA is also filled with the directory record containing the) 1689 SB
225 464 1671 (        matching entry, and the relative starting position is A * 32 \(that is, rotate the A) 1671 SB
225 523 1696 (        register left 5 bits, or ADD A five times\).  Although it is not usually required for) 1696 SB
225 582 1744 (        application programs, the directory information can be extracted from the buffer at) 1744 SB
225 641 359 (        this position.) 359 SB
225 760 1728 (          If the directory has been initialized for date and time stamping by INITDIR, then) 1728 SB
225 819 1769 (        an SFCB resides in every fourth directory entry, and successful Directory Codes are) 1769 SB
225 878 1687 (        restricted to the values 0 to 2. For successful searches, if the matching directory) 1687 SB
225 937 1767 (        record is an extent zero entry, and if an SFCB resides at offset 96 within the current) 1767 SB
225 996 1700 (        DMA, contents of \(DMA Address + 96\) = 21H, the SFCB contains the date and) 1700 SB
225 1055 1774 (        time stamp information, and password mode for the file.  This information is located) 1774 SB
225 1115 1665 (        at the relative starting position of 97 + \(A * 10\) within the current DMA in the) 1665 SB
225 1174 451 (        following format:) 451 SB
225 1292 1185 (            0 - 3   Create or Access Date and Time Stamp Field) 1185 SB
225 1351 991 (            4 - 7   Update Date and Time Stamp Field) 991 SB
225 1410 706 (            8 :     Password Mode Field) 706 SB
225 1529 1270 (          \(Refer to Section 2.3.8 for more information on SFCBS.\)) 1270 SB
225 1647 1717 (          If a physical error is encountered, the Search function performs different actions) 1717 SB
225 1706 1806 (        depending on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is in) 1806 SB
225 1765 1773 (        the default mode, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console, and the) 1773 SB
225 1825 1758 (        calling program is terminated.  Otherwise, the Search function returns to the calling) 1758 SB
225 1884 1690 (        program with register A set to OFFH, and register H set to one of the following) 1690 SB
225 1943 516 (        physical error codes:) 516 SB
225 2061 529 (            01   Disk I/O error) 529 SB
225 2120 619 (            04    Invalid drive error) 619 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-25) 92 SB
