225 227 1240 (                               BDOS FUNCTION 19: DELETE FILE) 1240 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 670 (                        Entry Parameters:) 670 SB
225 405 720 (                             Registers C: 13H) 720 SB
225 464 908 (                                          DE: FCB Address) 908 SB
225 582 639 (                        Returned Value:) 639 SB
225 641 945 (                             Registers A: Directory Code) 945 SB
225 700 1175 (                                            H: Extended or Physical Error) 1175 SB
225 878 1774 (           The Delete File function removes files or XFCBs that match the FCB addressed in) 1774 SB
225 937 1814 (         register pair DE.  The filename and filetype can contain ambiguous references, that is,) 1814 SB
225 996 1709 (         question marks 'in bytes fl through t3, but the dr byte cannot be ambiguous, as it) 1709 SB
225 1055 1802 (         can in the Search and Search Next functions.  Interface attribute f5' specifies the type) 1802 SB
225 1115 856 (         of delete operation that is performed.) 856 SB
225 1233 965 (             f5' = 0 - Standard Delete \(default mode\)) 965 SB
225 1292 727 (             f5' = 1 - Delete only XFCBs) 727 SB
225 1410 1812 (         If any of the files that the referenced FCB specify are password protected, the correct) 1812 SB
225 1470 1772 (         password must be placed in the first eight bytes of the current DMA buffer, or have) 1772 SB
225 1529 1534 (         been previously established as the default password \(see Function 106\).) 1534 SB
225 1647 1727 (           For standard delete operations, the Delete function removes all directory entries) 1727 SB
225 1706 1769 (         belonging to files that match the referenced FCB.  All disk directory and data space) 1769 SB
225 1765 1763 (         owned by the deleted files is returned to free space, and becomes available for allo-) 1763 SB
225 1825 1786 (         cation to other files.  Directory XFCBs that were owned by the deleted files are also) 1786 SB
225 1884 1800 (         removed from the directory.  If interface attribute f5' of the FCB is set to 1, Function) 1800 SB
225 1943 1478 (         19 deletes only the directory XFCBs that match the referenced FCB.) 1478 SB
225 2061 1700 (         Note: if any of the files that match the input FCB specification fall the password) 1700 SB
225 2120 1833 (         check, or are Read-Only, then the Delete function does not delete any files or XFCBS.) 1833 SB
225 2180 1045 (         This applies to both types of delete operations.) 1045 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-27) 92 SB
