225 227 1684 (     In nonbanked systems, file passwords and XFCBs are not supported.  Thus, if the) 1684 SB
225 286 1661 (   Delete function is called with interface attribute f5' set to true, the Delete function) 1661 SB
225 345 1189 (   performs no action but returns with register A set to zero.) 1189 SB
225 464 1656 (     Upon return, the Delete function returns a Directory Code in register A with the) 1656 SB
225 523 1696 (   value 0 if the delete is successful, or OFFH, 255 Decimal, if no file that matches the) 1696 SB
225 582 1773 (   referenced FCB is found.  Register H is set to zero in both of these cases.  If a physical,) 1773 SB
225 641 1616 (   or extended error is encountered, the Delete function performs different actions) 1616 SB
225 700 1692 (   depending on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is) 1692 SB
225 760 1695 (   the default mode, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console and the) 1695 SB
225 819 1687 (   calling program is terminated.  Otherwise, the Delete function returns to the calling) 1687 SB
225 878 1612 (   program with register A set to OFFH and register H set to one of the following) 1612 SB
225 937 699 (   physical or extended error codes:) 699 SB
225 1055 478 (        01 : Disk I/O error) 478 SB
225 1115 502 (        02 : Read-Only disk) 502 SB
225 1174 482 (        03 : Read-Only file) 482 SB
225 1233 555 (        04 : Invalid drive error) 555 SB
225 1292 581 (        07 : File password error) 581 SB
