225 227 1339 (                           BDOS FUNCTION 20: READ SEQUENTIAL) 1339 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 657 (                       Entry Parameters:) 657 SB
225 405 720 (                             Registers C: 14H) 720 SB
225 464 908 (                                          DE: FCB Address) 908 SB
225 582 626 (                       Returned Value:) 626 SB
225 641 863 (                             Registers A: Error Code) 863 SB
225 700 918 (                                            H: Physical Error) 918 SB
225 878 1755 (          The Read Sequential function reads the next 1 to 128 128-byte records from a file) 1755 SB
225 937 1783 (       into memory beginning at the current DMA address.  The BDOS Multi-Sector Count) 1783 SB
225 996 1724 (       \(see Function 44\) determines the number of records to be read.  The default is one) 1724 SB
225 1055 1771 (       record.  The FCB addressed by register pair DE must have been previously activated) 1771 SB
225 1115 769 (       by an Open or Make function call.) 769 SB
225 1233 1640 (          Function 20 reads each record from byte cr of the extent, then automatically) 1640 SB
225 1292 1761 (       increments the cr field to the next record position.  If the cr field overflows, then the) 1761 SB
225 1351 1689 (       function automatically opens the next logical extent and resets the cr field to 0 in) 1689 SB
225 1410 1759 (       preparation for the next read operation.  The calling program must set the cr field to) 1759 SB
225 1470 1715 (       0 following the Open call if the intent is to read sequentially from the beginning of) 1715 SB
225 1529 239 (       the file.) 239 SB
225 1647 1757 (          Upon return, the Read Sequential function sets register A to zero if the read oper-) 1757 SB
225 1706 1776 (       ation is successful.  Otherwise, register A contains an error code identifying the error) 1776 SB
225 1765 421 (       as shown below:) 421 SB
225 1884 975 (              01  Reading unwritten data \(end-of-file\)) 975 SB
225 1943 500 (              09  Invalid FCB) 500 SB
225 2002 724 (              10  Media change occurred) 724 SB
225 2061 937 (             255  Physical Error; refer to register H) 937 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-29) 92 SB
225 92 861 (BDOS Function Calls                                 ) 861 SB
1605 92 570 (CP/M 3 Programmers Guide) 570 SB
