32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 670 (                        Entry Parameters:) 670 SB
225 405 733 (                              Registers C: 15H) 733 SB
225 464 921 (                                           DE: FCB Address) 921 SB
225 582 639 (                        Returned Value:) 639 SB
225 641 876 (                              Registers A: Error Code) 876 SB
225 700 931 (                                             H: Physical Error) 931 SB
225 878 1757 (          The Write Sequential function writes 1 to 128 128-byte data records, beginning at) 1757 SB
225 937 1740 (        the current DMA address into the file named by the FCB addressed in register pair) 1740 SB
225 996 1791 (        DE. The BDOS Multi-Sector Count \(see Function 44\) determines the number of 128) 1791 SB
225 1055 1754 (        byte records that are written.  The default is one record.  The referenced FCB must) 1754 SB
225 1115 1524 (        have been previously activated by a BDOS Open or Make function call.) 1524 SB
225 1233 1728 (          Function 21 places the record into the file at the position indicated by the cr byte) 1728 SB
225 1292 1728 (        of the FCB, and then automatically increments the cr byte to the next record posi-) 1728 SB
225 1351 1750 (        tion.  If the cr field overflows, the function automatically opens, or creates the next) 1750 SB
225 1410 1773 (        logical extent, and resets the cr field to 0 in preparation for the next write operation.) 1773 SB
225 1470 1687 (        If Function 21 is used to write to an existing file, then the newly written records) 1687 SB
225 1529 1785 (        overlay those already existing in the file.  The calling program must set the cr field to) 1785 SB
225 1588 1652 (        0 following an Open or Make call if the intent is to write sequentially from the) 1652 SB
225 1647 511 (        beginning of the file.) 511 SB
225 1765 1755 (          Function 21 makes an Update date and time for the file if the following conditions) 1755 SB
225 1825 1717 (        are satisfied: the referenced drive has a directory label that requests date and time) 1717 SB
225 1884 1745 (        stamping, and the file has not already been stamped for update by a previous Make) 1745 SB
225 1943 542 (        or Write function call.) 542 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-31) 92 SB
