225 227 1144 (                           BDOS FUNCTION 22: MAKE FILE) 1144 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 592 (                  Entry Parameters:) 592 SB
225 405 655 (                        Registers C: 16H) 655 SB
225 464 843 (                                     DE: FCB Address) 843 SB
225 582 561 (                  Returned Value:) 561 SB
225 641 893 (                         Registers A: Directory Code) 893 SB
225 700 1123 (                                        H: Physical or Extended Error) 1123 SB
225 878 1653 (     The Make File function creates a new directory entry for a file under the current) 1653 SB
225 937 1708 (   user number.  It also creates an XFCB for the file if the referenced drive has a direc-) 1708 SB
225 996 1636 (   tory label that enables password protection on the drive, and the calling program) 1636 SB
225 1055 631 (   assigns a password to the file.) 631 SB
225 1174 1703 (     The calling program passes the address of the FCB in register pair DE, with byte 0) 1703 SB
225 1233 1607 (   of the FCB specifying the drive, bytes 1 through 11 specifying the filename and) 1607 SB
225 1292 1696 (   filctype, and byte 12 set to the extent number.  Usually, byte 12 is set to zero.  Byte) 1696 SB
225 1351 1705 (   32 of the FCB, the cr field, must be initialized to zero, before or after the Make call,) 1705 SB
225 1410 1326 (   if the intent is to write sequentially from the beginning of the file.) 1326 SB
225 1529 1697 (     Interface attribute f6' specifies whether a password is to be assigned to the created) 1697 SB
225 1588 113 (   file.) 113 SB
225 1706 933 (        f6' = 0 - Do not assign password \(default\)) 933 SB
225 1765 896 (        f6' = 1 - Assign password to created file) 896 SB
225 1884 1636 (   When attribute f6' is set to 1, the calling program must place the password in the) 1636 SB
225 1943 1629 (   first 8 bytes of the current DMA buffer, and set byte 9 of the DMA buffer to the) 1629 SB
225 2002 1687 (   password mode \(see Function 102\).  Note that the Make function only interrogates) 1687 SB
225 2061 1633 (   interface attribute f6' if passwords are activated on the referenced drive.  In non-) 1633 SB
225 2120 1792 (   banked systems, file passwords are not supported, and attribute f6' is never interrogated.) 1792 SB
225 2239 1656 (      The Make function returns with an error if the referenced FCB names a file that) 1656 SB
225 2298 1281 (   currently exists in the directory under the current user number.) 1281 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-34) 92 SB
225 92 861 (BDOS Function Calls                                 ) 861 SB
1605 92 570 (CP/M 3 Programmers Guide) 570 SB
