225 227 1748 (            If the Make function is successful, it activates the referenced FCB for file opera-) 1748 SB
225 286 1792 (          tions by opening the FCB, and initializes both the directory entry and the referenced) 1792 SB
225 345 1846 (          FCB to an empty file.  It also initializes all file attributes to zero.  In addition, Function) 1846 SB
225 405 1774 (          22 makes a Creation date and time stamp for the file if the following conditions are) 1774 SB
225 464 1754 (          satisfied: the referenced drive has a directory label that requests Creation date and) 1754 SB
225 523 1754 (          time stamping and the FCB extent number field is equal to zero.  Function 22 also) 1754 SB
225 582 1794 (          makes an Update stamp if the directory label requests update stamping and the FCB) 1794 SB
225 641 681 (          extent field is equal to zero.) 681 SB
225 760 1784 (            If the referenced drive contains a directory label that enables password protection,) 1784 SB
225 819 1752 (          and if interface attribute f6' has been set to 1, the Make function creates an XFCB) 1752 SB
225 878 1797 (          for the file.  In addition, Function 22 also assigns the password, and password mode) 1797 SB
225 937 1235 (          placed in the first nine bytes of the DMA, to the XFCB.) 1235 SB
225 1055 1709 (            Upon return, the Make function returns a directory code in register A with the) 1709 SB
225 1115 1750 (          value 0 if the make operation is successful, or OFFH, 25S decimal, if no directory) 1750 SB
225 1174 1760 (          space is available.  Register H is set to zero in both of these cases.  If a physical or) 1760 SB
225 1233 1808 (          extended error is encountered, the Make function performs different actions depend-) 1808 SB
225 1292 1714 (          ing on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is the) 1714 SB
225 1351 1725 (          default mode, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console, and the) 1725 SB
225 1410 1762 (          calling program is terminated.  Otherwise, the Make function returns to the calling) 1762 SB
225 1470 1716 (          program with register A set to OFFH, and register H set to one of the following) 1716 SB
225 1529 790 (          physical or extended error codes:) 790 SB
225 1647 569 (               01 : Disk I/O error) 569 SB
225 1706 593 (               02 : Read-Only disk) 593 SB
225 1765 646 (               04 : Invalid drive error) 646 SB
225 1825 638 (               08 : File already exists) 638 SB
225 1884 848 (               09 : ? in filename or filetype field) 848 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-35) 92 SB
