225 878 1660 (     The Rename function uses the FCB, addressed by register pair DE, to change all) 1660 SB
225 937 1691 (   directory entries of the file specified by the filename in the first 16 bytes of the FCB) 1691 SB
225 996 1640 (   to the filename in the second 16 bytes.  If the file specified by the first filename is) 1640 SB
225 1055 1677 (   password protected, the correct password must be placed in the first eight bytes of) 1677 SB
225 1115 1719 (   the current DMA buffer, or have been previously established as the default password) 1719 SB
225 1174 1743 (   \(see Function 106\).  The calling program must also ensure that the filenames specified) 1743 SB
225 1233 1671 (   in the FCB are valid and unambiguous, and that the new filename does not already) 1671 SB
225 1292 1665 (   exist on the drive.  Function 23 uses the dr code at byte 0 of the FCB to select the) 1665 SB
225 1351 1141 (   drive.  The drive code at byte 16 of the FCB is ignored.) 1141 SB
