225 760 1711 (      Function 24   returns the login vector in register pair HL. The login vector is a 16-) 1711 SB
225 819 1685 (     bit value with the least significant bit of L corresponding to drive A, and the high-) 1685 SB
225 878 1709 (     order bit of H corresponding to the 16th drive, labelled P. A 0 bit indicates that the) 1709 SB
225 937 1733 (     drive is not on-line, while a 1 bit indicates the drive is active.  A drive is made active) 1733 SB
225 996 1751 (     by either an explicit BDOS Select Disk call, number 14, or an implicit selection when) 1751 SB
225 1055 1774 (     a BDOS file operation specifies a non-zero dr byte in the FCB.  Function 24 maintains) 1774 SB
225 1115 1665 (     compatibilty with earlier releases since registers A and L contain the same values) 1665 SB
225 1174 311 (     upon return.) 311 SB
