225 227 1280 (                       BDOS FUNCTION 26: SET DMA ADDRESS) 1280 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 605 (                   Entry Parameters:) 605 SB
225 405 678 (                         Registers C: 1AH) 678 SB
225 464 865 (                                     DE: DMA Address) 865 SB
225 641 1671 (      DMA is an acronym for Direct Memory Address, which is often used in connec-) 1671 SB
225 700 1747 (     tion with disk controllers that directly access the memory of the computer to transfer) 1747 SB
225 760 1677 (     data to and from the disk subsystem.  Under CP/M 3, the current DMA is usually) 1677 SB
225 819 1737 (     defined as the buffer in memory where a record resides before a disk write, and after) 1737 SB
225 878 1760 (     a disk read operation.  If the BDOS Multi-Sector Count is equal to one \(see Function) 1760 SB
225 937 1757 (     44\), the size of the buffer is 128 bytes.  However, if the BDOS Multi-Sector Count is) 1757 SB
225 996 1633 (     greater than one, the size of the buffer must equal N * 128, where N equals the) 1633 SB
225 1055 469 (     Multi-Sector Count.) 469 SB
225 1174 1740 (       Some BDOS functions also use the current DMA to pass parameters, and to return) 1740 SB
225 1233 1712 (     values.  For example, BDOS functions that check and assign file passwords require) 1712 SB
225 1292 1733 (     that the password be placed in the current DMA.  As another example, Function 46,) 1733 SB
225 1351 1763 (     Get Disk Free Space, returns its results in the first 3 bytes of the current DMA. When) 1763 SB
225 1410 1683 (     the current DMA is used in this context, the size of the buffer in memory is deter-) 1683 SB
225 1470 1196 (     mined by the specific requirements of the called function.) 1196 SB
225 1588 1671 (       When a transient program is initiated by the CCP,       its DMA address is set to) 1671 SB
225 1647 1684 (     0080H.  The BDOS Reset Disk System function, Function 13, also sets the DMA) 1684 SB
225 1706 1715 (     address to 0080H.  The Set DMA function can change this default value to another) 1715 SB
225 1765 1766 (     memory address.  The DMA address is set to the value passed in the register pair DE.) 1766 SB
225 1825 1640 (     The DMA address remains at this value until it is changed by another Set DMA) 1640 SB
225 1884 776 (     Address, or Reset Disk System call.) 776 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-40) 92 SB
