225 760 1747 (          CP/M 3 maintains an allocation vector in main memory for each active disk drive.) 1747 SB
225 819 1745 (        Some programs use the information provided by the allocation vector to determine) 1745 SB
225 878 1742 (        the amount of free data space on a drive.  Note, however, that the allocation infor-) 1742 SB
225 937 1452 (        mation might be inaccurate if the drive has been marked Read-Only.) 1452 SB
225 1055 1721 (          Function 27 returns in register pair HL, the base address of the allocation vector) 1721 SB
225 1115 1741 (        for the currently selected drive.  If a physical error is encountered when the BDOS) 1741 SB
225 1174 1712 (        error mode is one of the return modes \(see Function 4S\), Function 27 returns the) 1712 SB
225 1233 868 (        value OFFFFH in the register pair HL.) 868 SB
225 1351 1713 (          In banked CP/M 3 systems, the allocation vector can be placed in bank zero.  In) 1713 SB
225 1410 1698 (        this case, a transient program cannot access the allocation vector.  However, the) 1698 SB
225 1470 1740 (        BDOS function, Get Disk Free Space \(Function 46\), can be used to directly return) 1740 SB
225 1529 1749 (        the number of free 128-byte records on a drive.  The CP/M 3 utilities that display a) 1749 SB
225 1588 1486 (        drive's free space, DIR and SHOW, use Function 46 for that purpose.) 1486 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-41) 92 SB
