225 996 1712 (       By calling the Set File Attributes function, a program can modify a file's attributes) 1712 SB
225 1055 1742 (    and set its last record byte count.  Other BDOS functions can be called to interrogate) 1742 SB
225 1115 1720 (    these file parameters, but only Function 30 can change them.  The file attributes that) 1720 SB
225 1174 1633 (    can be set or reset by Function 30 are fl' through f4', Read-Only, tl', System, t2',) 1633 SB
225 1233 1714 (    and Archive, t3'.  The register pair DE addresses an FCB containing a filename with) 1714 SB
225 1292 1711 (    the appropriate attributes set or reset.  The calling program must ensure that it does) 1711 SB
225 1351 1706 (     not specify an ambiguous filename.  In addition, if the specified file is password to-) 1706 SB
225 1410 1649 (    tected, the correct password must be placed in the first eight bytes of the current) 1649 SB
225 1470 1711 (    DMA buffer or have been previously established as the default password \(see Func-) 1711 SB
225 1529 247 (    tion 106\).) 247 SB
225 1647 1696 (       Interface attribute f6' specifies whether the last record byte count of the specified) 1696 SB
225 1706 353 (    file is to be set:) 353 SB
225 1825 1024 (         f6' = 0 - Do not set byte count \(default mode\)) 1024 SB
225 1884 574 (         f6' = 1 - Set byte count) 574 SB
225 2002 1687 (    If interface attribute f6' is set, the calling program must set the cr field of the refer-) 1687 SB
225 2061 1693 (    enced FCB to the byte count value.  A program can access a file's byte count value) 1693 SB
225 2120 1175 (    with the BDOS Open, Search, or Search Next functions.) 1175 SB
225 2239 1701 (       Function 30 searches the referenced directory for entries belonging to the current) 1701 SB
225 2298 1735 (    user number that matches the FCB specified name and type fields.  The function then) 1735 SB
225 2357 1698 (    updates the directory to contain the selected indicators, and if interface attribute f6') 1698 SB
225 2416 1681 (    is set, the specified byte count value.  Note that the last record byte count is main-) 1681 SB
225 2475 910 (    tained in byte 13 of a file's directory FCBS.) 910 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-44) 92 SB
225 92 861 (BDOS Function Calls                                 ) 861 SB
