225 641 798 (                        Registers A: Error Code) 798 SB
225 700 853 (                                       H: Physical Error) 853 SB
225 878 1672 (     The Read Random function is similar to the Read Sequential function except that) 1672 SB
225 937 1707 (   the read operation takes place at a particular random record number, selected by the) 1707 SB
225 996 1653 (   24-bit value constructed from the three byte, rO, rl, r2, field beginning at position) 1653 SB
225 1055 1691 (   33 of the FCB.  Note that the sequence of 24 bits is stored with the least significant) 1691 SB
225 1115 1713 (   byte first, rO, the middle byte next, rl, and the high byte last, r2.  The random record) 1713 SB
225 1174 1703 (   number can range from 0 to 262,143.  This corresponds to a maximum value of 3 in) 1703 SB
225 1233 191 (   byte r2.) 191 SB
225 1351 1576 (     To read a file with Function 33, the calling program must first open the base) 1576 SB
225 1410 1620 (   extent, extent 0. This ensures that the FCB is properly initialized for subsequent) 1620 SB
225 1470 1656 (   random access operations.  The base extent may or may not contain any allocated) 1656 SB
225 1529 1624 (   data.  Function 33 reads the record specified by the random record field into the) 1624 SB
225 1588 1721 (   current DMA address.  The function automatically sets the logical extent and current) 1721 SB
225 1647 1597 (   record values, but unlike the Read Sequential function, it does not advance the) 1597 SB
225 1706 1624 (   current record number.  Thus, a subsequent Read Random call rereads the same) 1624 SB
225 1765 1680 (   record.  After a random read operation, a file can be accessed sequentially, starting) 1680 SB
225 1825 1695 (   from the current randomly accessed position.  However, the last randomly accessed) 1695 SB
225 1884 1593 (   record is reread or rewritten when switching from random to sequential mode.) 1593 SB
225 2002 1664 (     If the BDOS Multi-Sector Count is greater than one \(see Function 44\), the Read) 1664 SB
225 2061 1674 (   Random function reads multiple consecutive records into memory beginning at the) 1674 SB
225 2120 1662 (   current DMA.  The rO, rl, and r2 field of the FCB is automatically incremented to) 1662 SB
225 2180 1711 (   read each record.  However, the FCBs random record number is restored to the first) 1711 SB
225 2239 1024 (   record's value upon return to the calling program.) 1024 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-48) 92 SB
