225 227 1752 (           Upon return, the Read Random function sets register A to zero if the read opera-) 1752 SB
225 286 1793 (        tion was  successful. Otherwise, register A contains one of the following error codes:) 1793 SB
225 405 988 (               01  Reading unwritten data \(end-of-file\)) 988 SB
225 464 819 (               03  Cannot close current extent) 819 SB
225 523 760 (               04  Seek to unwritten extent) 760 SB
225 582 998 (               06  Random record number out of range) 998 SB
225 641 737 (               10  Media change occurred) 737 SB
225 700 964 (              255  Physical Error : refer to register H) 964 SB
225 819 1732 (           Error Code 01 is returned if no data exists at the next record position of the file.) 1732 SB
225 878 1711 (        Usually, the no data situation is encountered at the end of a file.  However, it can) 1711 SB
225 937 1709 (        also occur if an attempt is made to read a data block that has not been previously) 1709 SB
225 996 258 (        written.) 258 SB
225 1115 1655 (           Error Code 03 is returned when the Read Random function cannot close the) 1655 SB
225 1174 1038 (        current extent prior to moving to a new extent.) 1038 SB
225 1292 1739 (           Error Code 04 is returned when a read random operation accesses an extent that) 1739 SB
225 1351 523 (        has not been created.) 523 SB
225 1470 1767 (           Error Code 06 is returned when byte 35, r2, of the referenced FCB is greater than) 1767 SB
225 1529 142 (        3.) 142 SB
225 1647 1710 (           Error Code 10 is returned if a media change occurs on the drive after the refer-) 1710 SB
225 1706 1209 (        enced FCB is activated by a BDOS Open or Make Call.) 1209 SB
225 1825 1771 (           Error Code 255 is returned if a physical error is encountered, and the BDOS error) 1771 SB
225 1884 1754 (        mode is one of the return modes \(see Function 45\).  If the error mode is the default) 1754 SB
225 1943 1722 (        mode, a message identifying the physical error is displayed at the console, and the) 1722 SB
225 2002 1749 (        calling program is terminated.  When a physical error is returned to the calling pro-) 1749 SB
225 2061 1273 (        gram, register H contains one of the following error codes:) 1273 SB
225 2180 542 (             01   Disk I/O error) 542 SB
225 2239 619 (             04   Invalid drive error) 619 SB
225 2357 1615 (           On all error returns except for physical errors, A = 255, the Read Random) 1615 SB
225 2416 1787 (        function sets register H to the number of records successfully read before the error is) 1787 SB
225 2475 1738 (        encountered.  This value can range from 0 to 127 depending on the current BDOS) 1738 SB
225 2535 1794 (        Multi-Sector Count.  It is always set to zero when the Multi-Sector Count is equal to) 1794 SB
225 2594 189 (        one.) 189 SB
