225 227 1248 (                         BDOS FUNCTION 34: WRITE RANDOM) 1248 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 618 (                    Entry Parameters:) 618 SB
225 405 681 (                          Registers C: 22H) 681 SB
225 464 869 (                                       DE: FCB Address) 869 SB
225 582 587 (                    Returned Value:) 587 SB
225 641 824 (                          Registers A: Error Code) 824 SB
225 700 879 (                                         H: Physical Error) 879 SB
225 878 1662 (       The Write Random function is analogous to the Read Random function, except) 1662 SB
225 937 1702 (    that data is written to the disk from the current DMA address.  If the disk extent or) 1702 SB
225 996 1694 (    data block where the data is to be written is not already allocated, the BDOS auto-) 1694 SB
225 1055 1445 (    matically performs the allocation before the write operation continues.) 1445 SB
225 1174 1710 (       To write to a file using the Write Random function, the calling program must first) 1710 SB
225 1233 1684 (    open the base extent, extent 0. This ensures that the FCB is properly initialized for) 1684 SB
225 1292 1714 (    subsequent random access operations.  If the file is empty, the calling program must) 1714 SB
225 1351 1691 (    create the base extent with the Make File function before calling Function 34.  The) 1691 SB
225 1410 1713 (    base extent might or might not contain any allocated data, but it does record the file) 1713 SB
225 1470 1373 (    in the directory, so that the file can be displayed by the DIR utility.) 1373 SB
225 1588 1716 (       The Write Random function sets the logical extent and current record positions to) 1716 SB
225 1647 1692 (    correspond with the random record being written, but does not change the random) 1692 SB
225 1706 1744 (    record number.  Thus, sequential read or write operations can follow a random write,) 1744 SB
225 1765 1651 (    with the current record being reread or rewritten as the calling program switches) 1651 SB
225 1825 712 (    from random to sequential mode.) 712 SB
225 1943 1629 (       Function 34 makes an Update date and time stamp for the file if the following) 1629 SB
225 2002 1761 (    conditions are satisfied: the referenced drive has a directory label that requests Update) 1761 SB
225 2061 1607 (    date and time stamping if the file has not already been stamped for update by a) 1607 SB
225 2120 769 (    previous BDOS Make or Write call.) 769 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-50) 92 SB
