225 227 1393 (                             BDOS FUNCTION 35: COMPUTE FILE SIZE) 1393 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 696 (                          Entry Parameters:) 696 SB
225 405 759 (                                Registers C: 23H) 759 SB
225 464 947 (                                             DE: FCB Address) 947 SB
225 582 665 (                          Returned Value:) 665 SB
225 641 882 (                                Registers A: Error Flag) 882 SB
225 700 1205 (                                               H: Physical or Extended error) 1205 SB
225 819 930 (                                Random Record Field Set) 930 SB
225 996 1766 (           The Compute File Size function determines the virtual file size, which is, in effect,) 1766 SB
225 1055 1767 (         the address of the record immediately following the end of the file.  The virtual size) 1767 SB
225 1115 1805 (         of a file corresponds to the physical size if the file is written sequentially.  If the file is) 1805 SB
225 1174 1744 (         written in random mode, gaps might exist in the allocation, and the file might con-) 1744 SB
225 1233 1813 (         tain fewer records than the indicated size.  For example, if a single record with record) 1813 SB
225 1292 1764 (         number 262,143, the CP/M 3 maximum is written to a file using the Write Random) 1764 SB
225 1351 1766 (         function, then the virtual size of the file is 262,144 records even though only 1 data) 1766 SB
225 1410 648 (         block 'is actually allocated.) 648 SB
225 1529 1767 (           To compute file size, the calling program passes in register pair DE the address of) 1767 SB
225 1588 1703 (         an FCB in random mode format, bytes rO, rl and r2 present.  Note that the FCB) 1703 SB
225 1647 1732 (         must contain an unambiguous filename and filetype.  Function 35 sets the random) 1732 SB
225 1706 1728 (         record field of the FCB to the random record number + 1 of the last record in the) 1728 SB
225 1765 1689 (         file.  If the r2 byte is set to 04, then the file contains the maximum record count) 1689 SB
225 1825 293 (         262,144.) 293 SB
225 1943 1766 (           A program can append data to the end of an existing file by calling Function 35 to) 1766 SB
225 2002 1776 (         set the random record position to the end of file, and then performing a sequence of) 1776 SB
225 2061 1138 (         random writes starting at the preset record address.) 1138 SB
225 2180 1811 (         Note: the BDOS does not require that the file be open to use Function 35.  However,) 1811 SB
225 2239 1745 (         if the file has been written to, it must be closed before calling Function 35.  Other-) 1745 SB
225 2298 1008 (         wise, an incorrect file size might be returned.) 1008 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-53) 92 SB
