225 819 1650 (     The Reset Drive function programmatically restores specified drives to the reset) 1650 SB
225 878 1735 (   state.  A reset drive is not logged-in and is in Read-Write status.  The passed parame-) 1735 SB
225 937 1702 (   ter in register pair DE is a 16-bit vector of drives to be reset, where the least signifi-) 1702 SB
225 996 1661 (   cant bit corresponds to the first drive A, and the high-order bit corresponds to the) 1661 SB
225 1055 1649 (   sixteenth drive, labelled P. Bit values of 1 indicate that the specified drive is to be) 1649 SB
225 1115 147 (   reset.) 147 SB
