225 227 1485 (                      BDOS FUNCTION 44: SET MULTI-SECTOR COUNT) 1485 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 657 (                       Entry Parameters:) 657 SB
225 405 728 (                             Registers C: 2CH) 728 SB
225 464 1007 (                                            E: Number of Sectors) 1007 SB
225 582 626 (                       Returned Value:) 626 SB
225 641 911 (                              Register   A: Return Code) 911 SB
225 819 1643 (          The Set Multi-Sector Count function provides logical record blocking under) 1643 SB
225 878 1753 (        CP/M 3. It enables a program to read and write from 1 to 128 records of 128 bytes) 1753 SB
225 937 1327 (        at a time during subsequent BDOS Read and Write functions.) 1327 SB
225 1055 1767 (          Function 44 sets the Multi-Sector Count value for the calling program to the value) 1767 SB
225 1115 1808 (        passed in register E. Once set, the specified Multi-Sector Count remains in effect until) 1808 SB
225 1174 1784 (        the calling program makes another Set Multi-Sector Count function call and changes) 1784 SB
225 1233 1756 (        the value.  Note that the CCP sets the Multi-Sector Count to one when it initiates a) 1756 SB
225 1292 469 (        transient program.) 469 SB
225 1410 1698 (          The Multi-Sector Count affects BDOS error reporting for the BDOS Read and) 1698 SB
225 1470 1825 (        Write functions.  If an error interrupts these functions when the Multi-Sector is greater) 1825 SB
225 1529 1736 (        than one, they return the number of records successfully read or written in register) 1736 SB
225 1588 1142 (        H for all errors except for physical errors \(A = 255\).) 1142 SB
225 1706 1719 (          Upon return, register A is set to zero if the specified value is in the range of 1 to) 1719 SB
225 1765 952 (        128.  Otherwise, register A is set to 0FFH.) 952 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-63) 92 SB
