225 227 1361 (                   BDOS FUNCTION 45: SET BDOS ERROR MODE) 1361 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 605 (                   Entry Parameters:) 605 SB
225 405 679 (                         Registers C: 2DH) 679 SB
225 464 962 (                                        E: BDOS Error Mode) 962 SB
225 582 734 (                      Returned Value: None) 734 SB
225 760 1709 (      Function 45 sets the BDOS error mode for the calling program to the mode speci-) 1709 SB
225 819 1706 (    fied in register E. If register E is set to OFFH, 255 decimal, the error mode is set to) 1706 SB
225 878 1720 (    Return Error mode.  If register E is set to OFEH, 254 decimal, the error mode is set) 1720 SB
225 937 1738 (    to Return and Display mode.  If register E is set to any other value, the error mode is) 1738 SB
225 996 521 (    set to the default mode.) 521 SB
225 1115 1737 (      The SET BDOS Error Mode function determines how physical and extended errors) 1737 SB
225 1174 1694 (    \(see Section 2.2.13\) are handled for a program.  The Error Mode can exist in three) 1694 SB
225 1233 1696 (    modes: the default mode, Return Error mode, and Return and Display Error mode.) 1696 SB
225 1292 1721 (    In the default mode, the BDOS displays a system message at the console that identi-) 1721 SB
225 1351 1756 (    fies the error and terminates the calling program.  In the return modes, the BDOS sets) 1756 SB
225 1410 1717 (    register A to OFFH, 255 decimal, places an error code that identifies the physical or) 1717 SB
225 1470 1604 (    extended error in register H and returns to the calling program.  In Return and) 1604 SB
225 1529 1731 (    Display mode, the BDOS displays the system message before returning to the calling) 1731 SB
225 1588 1731 (    program.  No system messages are displayed, however, when the BDOS is in Return) 1731 SB
225 1647 296 (    Error mode.) 296 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-64) 92 SB
