225 641 1741 (           The Chain To Program function provides a means of chaining from one program) 1741 SB
225 700 1744 (         to the next without operator intervention.  The calling program must place a com-) 1744 SB
225 760 1809 (         mand line terminated by a null byte, OOH, in the default DMA buffer.  If register E is) 1809 SB
225 819 1707 (         set to 0FFH, the CCP initializes the default drive and user number to the current) 1707 SB
225 878 1811 (         program values when it passes control to the specified transient program.  Otherwise,) 1811 SB
225 937 1795 (         these parameters are set to the default CCP values.  Note that Function 108, Get/Set) 1795 SB
225 996 1793 (         Program Return Code, can be used to pass a two byte value to the chained program.) 1793 SB
225 1115 1707 (           Function 47 does not return any values to the calling program and any encoun-) 1707 SB
225 1174 844 (         tered errors are handled by the CCP.) 844 SB
