225 700 840 (                                      H: Physical Error) 840 SB
225 878 1698 (    The Flush Buffers function forces the write of any write-pending records contained) 1698 SB
225 937 1747 (   in internal blocking/deblocking buffers.  If register E is set to OFFH, this function also) 1747 SB
225 996 1696 (   purges all active data buffers.  Programs that provide write with read verify support) 1696 SB
225 1055 1700 (   need to purge internal buffers  to ensure that verifying reads actually access the disk) 1700 SB
225 1115 1654 (   instead of returning data that is resident in internal data buffers.  The CP/M 3 PIP) 1654 SB
225 1174 820 (   utility is an example of such a program.) 820 SB
225 1292 1612 (     Upon return, register A is    set to zero if the flush operation is successful. If a) 1612 SB
225 1351 1690 (   physical error is encountered,  the Flush Buffers function performs different actions) 1690 SB
225 1410 1741 (   depending on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is in) 1741 SB
225 1470 1708 (   the default mode,, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console and the) 1708 SB
225 1529 1682 (   calling program is terminated.  Otherwise, the Flush Buffers function returns to the) 1682 SB
225 1588 1615 (   calling program with register A set to OFFH and register H set to the following) 1615 SB
225 1647 432 (   physical error code:) 432 SB
225 1765 464 (       0 1  Disk I/O error) 464 SB
225 1825 475 (       02   Read/only disk) 475 SB
225 1884 541 (       04   Invalid drive error) 541 SB
