225 937 1705 (          Function 49 allows access to parameters located in the CP/M 3 System Control) 1705 SB
225 996 1742 (       Block \(SCB\).  The SCB is a 100-byte data structure residing within the BDOS that) 1742 SB
225 1055 1786 (       contains flags and data used by the BDOS, CCP and other system components.  Note) 1786 SB
225 1115 1796 (       that Function 49 is a CP/M 3 specific function.  Programs intended for both MP/M 11) 1796 SB
225 1174 1623 (       and CP/M 3 should either avoid the use of this function or isolate calls to this) 1623 SB
225 1233 1036 (       function in CP/M 3 version-dependent sections.) 1036 SB
225 1351 1679 (          To use Function 49, the calling program passes the address of a data structure) 1679 SB
225 1410 1778 (       called the SCB parameter block in register pair DE.  This data structure identifies the) 1778 SB
225 1470 1705 (       byte or word of the SCB to be updated or returned.  The SCB parameter block is) 1705 SB
225 1529 304 (       defined as:) 304 SB
225 1647 1264 (       SCBPB:             DB OFFSET             ;  Offset within SCB) 1264 SB

