225 227 1733 (      Use caution when you set SCB fields.  Some of these parameters reflect the current) 1733 SB
225 286 1665 (   state of the operating system.  If they are set to invalid values, software errors can) 1665 SB
225 345 1738 (   result.  In general, do not use Function 49 to set a system parameter if another BDOS) 1738 SB
225 405 1626 (   function can achieve the same result.  For example, Function 49 can be called to) 1626 SB
225 464 1649 (   update the Current DMA Address field within the SCB.  This is not equivalent to) 1649 SB
225 523 1703 (   making a Function 26, Set DMA Address call, and updating the SCB Current DMA) 1703 SB
225 582 1726 (   field in this way would result in system errors.  However, you can use Function 49 to) 1726 SB
225 641 1677 (   return the Current DMA address.  The System Control Block is summarized in the) 1677 SB
