975 1292 434 (; HL register contents) 434 SB
225 1410 1635 (      System Reset \(Function  0\) is equivalent to Function 50 with a BIOS  function) 1635 SB
225 1470 306 (    number of 1.) 306 SB
225 1588 1727 (      Note that the register pair BIOSPB fields \(BCREG, DEREG, HLREG\) arc defined) 1727 SB
225 1647 1752 (    in low byte, high byte order.  For example, in the BCREG field, the first byte contains) 1752 SB
225 1706 1364 (    the C register value, the second byte contains the B register value.) 1364 SB
225 1825 1716 (      Under CP/M 3, direct BIOS calls via the BIOS jump vector are only supported for) 1716 SB
225 1884 1762 (    the BIOS Console I/O and List functions.  You must use Function 50 to call any other) 1762 SB
225 1943 1747 (    BIOS functions.  In addition, Function 50 intercepts BIOS Function 27 \(Select Mem-) 1747 SB
225 2002 1661 (    ory\) calls and returns with register A set to zero.  Refer to the CPIM Plus \(CP/M) 1661 SB
225 2061 1716 (    Version 3\) Operating System System Guide for the definition of the BIOS functions) 1716 SB
225 2120 1028 (    and their register passing and return conventions.) 1028 SB
