225 227 1317 (                               BDOS FUNCTION 59: LOAD OVERLAY) 1317 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 696 (                          Entry Parameters:) 696 SB
225 405 767 (                                Registers C: 3BH) 767 SB
225 464 947 (                                             DE: FCB Address) 947 SB
225 582 665 (                          Returned Value:) 665 SB
225 641 902 (                                Registers A: Error Code) 902 SB
225 700 970 (                                                H: Physical Error) 970 SB
225 878 1757 (             Only transient programs with an RSX header can use the Load Overlay function) 1757 SB
225 937 1803 (          because BDOS Function 59 is supported by the LOADER module.  The calling pro-) 1803 SB
225 996 1812 (          gram must have a header to force the LOADER to remain resident after the program) 1812 SB
225 1055 667 (          is loaded \(see Section 1.3\).) 667 SB
225 1174 1781 (             Function 59 loads either an absolute or relocatable module.  Relocatable modules) 1781 SB
225 1233 1772 (             are identified by a filetype of PRL.  Function 59 does not call the loaded module.) 1772 SB
225 1351 1824 (             The referenced FCB must be successfully opened before Function 59 is called.  The) 1824 SB
225 1410 1786 (          load address is specified in the first two random record bytes of the FCB, rO and rl.) 1786 SB
225 1470 1811 (          The LOADER returns an error if the load address is less than 100H, or if performing) 1811 SB
225 1529 1733 (          the requested load operation would overlay the LOADER, or any other Resident) 1733 SB
225 1588 1178 (          System Extensions that have been previously loaded.) 1178 SB
225 1706 1816 (             When loading relocatable files, the LOADER requires enough room at the load ad-) 1816 SB
225 1765 1781 (          dress for the complete PRL file including the header and bit map \(see Appendix B\).) 1781 SB
225 1825 1759 (          Otherwise an error is returned.  Function 59 also returns an error on PRL file load) 1759 SB
225 1884 1394 (          requests if the specified load address is not on a page boundary.) 1394 SB
225 2002 1813 (             Upon return, Function 59 sets register A to zero if the load operation is successful.) 1813 SB
225 2061 1795 (          If the LOADER RSX is not resident in memory because the calling program did not) 1795 SB
225 2120 1833 (          have a RSX header, the BDOS returns with register A set to OFFH and register H set) 1833 SB
225 2180 1804 (          to zero.  If the LOADER detects an invalid load address, or if insufficient memory is) 1804 SB
225 2239 1777 (          available to load the overlay, Function 59 returns with register A set to OFEH.  All) 1777 SB
225 2298 1770 (          other error returns are consistent with the error codes returned by BDOS Function) 1770 SB
225 2357 541 (          20, Read Sequential.) 541 SB
