225 819 1680 (          The Free Blocks function scans all the currently logged-in drives, and for each) 1680 SB
225 878 1776 (        drive returns to free space all temporarily-allocated data blocks.  A temporarily-allo-) 1776 SB
225 937 1612 (        cated data block is a block that has been allocated to a file by a BDOS write) 1612 SB
225 996 1746 (        operation but has not been permanently recorded in the directory by a BDOS close) 1746 SB
225 1055 1738 (        operation.  The CCP calls Function 98 when it receives control following a system) 1738 SB
225 1115 1782 (        warm start.  Be sure to close your file, particularly any file you have written to, prior) 1782 SB
225 1174 551 (        to calling Function 98.) 551 SB
225 1292 1757 (          In the nonbanked version of CP/M 3, Function 98 frees only temporarily allocated) 1757 SB
225 1351 1511 (        blocks for systems that request double allocation vectors in GENCPM.) 1511 SB
225 1470 1690 (          Upon return, register A is set to zero if Function 98 is successful.  If a physical) 1690 SB
225 1529 1759 (        error is encountered, the Free Blocks function performs different actions depending) 1759 SB
225 1588 1812 (        on the BDOS error mode \(see Function 45\).  If the BDOS error mode is in the default) 1812 SB
225 1647 1679 (        mode, a message identifying the error is displayed at the console and the calling) 1679 SB
225 1706 1719 (        program is terminated.  Otherwise, the Free Blocks function returns to the calling) 1719 SB
