225 996 1647 (    the FCB in register pair DE, with byte 0 of the FCB specifying the drive, bytes 1) 1647 SB
225 1055 1718 (    through 11 specifying the filename and filetype, and bytes 33 through 35, rO, rl, and) 1718 SB
225 1115 1687 (    r2, specifying the last record number of the file.  The last record number is a 24 bit) 1687 SB
225 1174 1720 (    value, stored with the least significant byte first, rO, the middle byte next, rl, and the) 1720 SB
225 1233 1694 (    high byte last, r2.  This value can range from 0 to 262,143, which corresponds to a) 1694 SB
225 1292 670 (    maximum value of 3 in byte r2.) 670 SB
225 1410 1710 (      If the file specified by the referenced FCB is password protected, the correct pass-) 1710 SB
225 1470 1727 (    word must be placed in the first eight bytes of the current DMA buffer, or have been) 1727 SB
225 1529 1364 (    previously established as the default password \(see Function 106\).) 1364 SB
225 1647 1689 (      Function 99 requires that the file specified by the FCB not be open, particularly if) 1689 SB
225 1706 1701 (    the file has been written to.  In addition, any activated FCBs naming the file are not) 1701 SB
225 1765 1730 (    valid after Function 99 is called.  Close your file before calling Function 99, and then) 1730 SB
225 1825 1172 (    reopen it after the call to continue processing on the file.) 1172 SB
