225 760 1743 (          The Set Default Password function allows a program to specify a password value) 1743 SB
225 819 1773 (        before a file protected by the password is accessed.  When the file system accesses a) 1773 SB
225 878 1797 (        password-protected file, it checks the current DMA, and the default password for the) 1797 SB
225 937 1703 (        correct value.  If either value matches the file's password, full access to the file is) 1703 SB
225 996 1748 (        allowed.  Note that this function performs no action in nonbanked CP/M 3 systems) 1748 SB
225 1055 932 (        because file passwords are not supported.) 932 SB
