225 937 1747 (          CP/M 3 allows programs to set a return code before terminating.  This provides a) 1747 SB
225 996 1708 (        mechanism for programs to pass an error code or value to a following job step in) 1708 SB
225 1055 1729 (        batch environments.  For example, Program Return Codes are used by the CCP in) 1729 SB
225 1115 1728 (        CP/M 3's conditional command line batch facility.  Conditional command lines are) 1728 SB
225 1174 1742 (        command lines that begin with a colon, :. The execution of a conditional command) 1742 SB
225 1233 1762 (        depends on the successful execution of the preceding command.  The CCP tests the) 1762 SB
225 1292 1784 (        return code of a terminating program to determine whether it successfully completed) 1784 SB
225 1351 1752 (        or terminated in error.  Program return codes can also be used by programs to pass) 1752 SB
225 1410 1749 (        an error code or value to a chained program \(see Function 47, Chain To Program\).) 1749 SB
225 1529 1700 (          A program can set or interrogate the Program Return Code by calling Function) 1700 SB
225 1588 1816 (        108.  If re 'ster pair DE = OFFFFH, then the current Program Return Code is returned) 1816 SB
225 1647 1744 (        in register pair HL.  Otherwise, Function 108 sets the Program Return Code to the) 1744 SB
225 1706 1798 (        'value contained in register pair DE.  Program Return Codes are defined in Table 3-5.) 1798 SB
