225 1115 1674 (           The Console Mode is a 16-bit system parameter that determines the action of) 1674 SB
225 1174 1641 (        certain BDOS Console I/O functions.  The definition of the Console Mode is:) 1641 SB
225 1292 1157 (              bit 0  = 1 - CTRL-C only status for Function 1 1.) 1157 SB
225 1351 1021 (                      = 0 - Normal status for Function 1 1.) 1021 SB
225 1470 1602 (              bit 1 =   1- Disable stop scroll, CTRL-S, start scroll, CTRL-Q, support.) 1602 SB
225 1529 1162 (                      =   0-Enable stop scroll, start scroll support.) 1162 SB
225 1647 1734 (              bit 2 =   1- Raw console output mode. Disables tab expansion for Functions 2,) 1734 SB
225 1706 1492 (                          9 and 111.  Also disables printer echo, CTIRL-P, support.) 1492 SB
225 1765 1015 (                      =   0 - Normal console output mode.) 1015 SB
225 1884 1177 (              bit 3 =   1 - Disable CTRL-C program termination) 1177 SB
225 1943 1167 (                      =   0 - Enable CTRL-C program termination) 1167 SB
