225 878 1704 (      The Parse Filename function parses an ASCII file specification and prepares a File) 1704 SB
225 937 1774 (    Control Block, FCB.  The calling program passes the address of a data structure called) 1774 SB
225 996 1763 (    the Parse Filename Control Block, PFCB, in register pair DE.  The PFCB contains the) 1763 SB
225 1055 1736 (    address of the input ASCII filename string followed by the address of the target FCB) 1736 SB
225 1115 382 (    as shown below:) 382 SB
225 1233 456 (    PFCB: DW INPUT ) 456 SB
825 1233 624 (; Address of input ASCII string) 624 SB
225 1292 513 (               DW FCB          ) 513 SB
825 1292 477 (; Address of target FCB) 477 SB
225 1410 1730 (    The maximum length of the input ASCII string to be parsed is 128 bytes.  The target) 1730 SB
225 1470 689 (    FCB must be 36 bytes in length.) 689 SB
225 1588 1685 (      Function 152 assumes the input string contains file specifications in the following) 1685 SB
225 1647 161 (    form:) 161 SB
225 1765 755 (        {d:}filename{.typll}{;password}) 755 SB
225 1884 1706 (    where items enclosed in curly brackets are optional.  Function 152 also accepts iso-) 1706 SB
225 1943 1679 (    lated drive specifications d: in the input string.  When it encounters one, it sets the) 1679 SB
225 2002 1223 (    filename, filetype, and password fields in the FCB to blank.) 1223 SB
