225 227 1730 (           The Parse Filename function parses the first file specification it finds in the input) 1730 SB
225 286 1859 (         string.  The function first eliminates leading blanks and tabs.  The function then assumes) 1859 SB
225 345 1655 (         that the file specification ends on the first delimiter it encounters that is out of) 1655 SB
225 405 1763 (         context with the specific field it is parsing.  For instance, if it finds a colon, and it is) 1763 SB
225 464 1716 (         not the second character of the file specification, the colon delimits the entire file) 1716 SB
225 523 378 (         specification.) 378 SB
225 641 1397 (           Function 152 recognizes the following characters as detimiters:) 1397 SB
225 760 292 (              space) 292 SB
225 819 243 (              tab) 243 SB
225 878 302 (              return) 302 SB
225 937 263 (              nut]) 263 SB
225 996 1055 (             ;  \(semicolon\) - except before password field) 1055 SB
225 1055 363 (              = \(equal\)) 363 SB
225 1115 427 (              < \(less than\)) 427 SB
225 1174 495 (              > \(greater than\)) 495 SB
225 1233 1207 (              . \(period\) - except after filename and before filetype) 1207 SB
225 1292 1145 (              : \(colon\) - except before filename and after drive) 1145 SB
225 1351 399 (              ,  \(comma\)) 399 SB
225 1410 461 (              | \(vertical bar\)) 461 SB
225 1470 613 (              [ \(left square bracket\)) 613 SB
225 1529 642 (              ] \(right square bracket\)) 642 SB
225 1647 1730 (         If Function 152 encounters a non-graphic character in the range 1 through 31 not) 1730 SB
225 1706 1825 (         listed above, it treats the character as an error.  The Parse Filename function initializes) 1825 SB
225 1765 879 (         the specified FCB shown in Table 3-6.) 879 SB
1154 2830 92 (3-97) 92 SB
