225 345 1685 (           On a successful parse, the Parse Filename function checks the next item in the) 1685 SB
225 405 1791 (         input string.  It skips over trailing blanks and tabs and looks at the next character.  If) 1791 SB
225 464 1784 (         the character is a null or carriage return, it returns a 0 indicating the end of the input) 1784 SB
225 523 1737 (         string.  If the character is a delimiter, it returns the address of the delimiter.  If the) 1737 SB
225 582 1719 (         character is not a delimiter, it returns the address of the first trailing blank or tab.) 1719 SB
225 700 1615 (           If the first non-blank or non-tab character in the input string is a null, 0, or) 1615 SB
225 760 1689 (         carriage return, the Parse Filename function returns a zero indicating the end of) 1689 SB
225 819 242 (         string.) 242 SB
