225 1943 1788 (          Note that this program   makes several simplifications and could be enhanced. First,) 1788 SB
225 2002 1727 (        it does not check for invalid filenames that could, for example, contain ambiguous) 1727 SB
225 2061 1705 (        references.  This situation could be detected by scanning the 32-byte default area) 1705 SB
225 2120 1745 (        starting at location 005CH for ASCII question marks.  To check that the filenames) 1745 SB
225 2180 1719 (        have, in fact, been included, COPY could check locations 005DH and 006DH for) 1719 SB
225 2239 1815 (        nonblank ASCII characters.  Finally, a check should be made to ensure that the source) 1815 SB
225 2298 1767 (        and destination filenames are different.  Speed could be improved by buffering more) 1767 SB
225 2357 1764 (        data on each read operation.  For example, you could determine the size of memory) 1764 SB
225 2416 1714 (        by fetching FBASE from location 0006H, and use the entire remaining portion of) 1714 SB
225 2475 1765 (        memory for a data buffer.  You could also use CP/M 3's Multi-Sector I/O facility to) 1765 SB
225 2535 871 (        read and write data in up to 16K units.) 871 SB
