225 227 606 (            4.4.1 The RSX Prefix) 606 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c33d font
225 345 1785 (             The first 27 bytes of an RSX program contain a standard data structure called the) 1785 SB
225 405 1247 (            RSX prefix.  The RSX prefix has the following format:) 1247 SB
375 523 235 (serial:         ) 235 SB
225 582 576 (                d b       0,0,0,0,0,0) 576 SB
225 641 271 (            start:.) 271 SB
225 700 451 (                         jmp    ) 451 SB
825 700 790 (ftest                           ; start of Program) 790 SB
225 760 307 (            n e x t :) 307 SB
225 819 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 819 850 (0c3h                           ; jump instruction to) 850 SB
225 878 477 (                         dw       ) 477 SB
825 878 844 ( 0                               ; next module in line) 844 SB
225 937 326 (            Prev:     ) 326 SB
525 996 178 (  dw       ) 178 SB
825 996 800 ( 0                               ; Previous module) 800 SB
225 1055 318 (            remove:) 318 SB
225 1115 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 1115 443 (0ffh                            ) 443 SB
1275 1115 261 (; remove flag) 261 SB
225 1174 339 (            nonbank:) 339 SB
225 1233 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 1233 428 (0                               ) 428 SB
1275 1233 282 (; nonbank flag) 282 SB
225 1292 275 (            name:) 275 SB
225 1351 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 1351 332 ('123456713'       ) 332 SB
1275 1351 459 (; any B-character name) 459 SB
225 1410 320 (            loade r :) 320 SB
225 1470 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 1470 324 (0                       ) 324 SB
1275 1470 237 (; loader flag) 237 SB
225 1529 478 (                         db        ) 478 SB
825 1529 743 (0,0                             ;  reserved area) 743 SB
225 1647 1827 (              The only   fields of the RSX prefix that you must initialize are the remove: flag, the) 1827 SB
225 1706 980 (            nonbank: flag, and the name: of the RSX.) 980 SB
225 1825 1776 (              For compatibility with previous releases of CP/M, the serial: field of the prefix is) 1776 SB
225 1884 1797 (            set to the serial number of the operating system by the LOADER module when the) 1797 SB
225 1943 1832 (            RSX is loaded into memory.  Thus, the address in location 6 locates the byte follow-) 1832 SB
225 2002 1733 (            ing the serial number of the operating system with or withou; RSXs in memory.) 1733 SB
225 2120 1700 (              The start: field contains a jump instruction to the beginning of the RSX code) 1700 SB
225 2180 1812 (            where the RSX tests to see if this BDOS function call is to be intercepted or passed) 1812 SB
225 2239 737 (            on to the next module in line.) 737 SB
225 2357 1774 (              The next: field contains a jump instruction to the next module in the chain or the) 1774 SB
225 2416 1817 (            LOADER module if the RSX is the oldest one in memory.  The RSX program must) 1817 SB
225 2475 1472 (            make its own BDOS function calls by calling the next: entry point.) 1472 SB
1154 2830 92 (4-21) 92 SB
225 92 742 (4.4 Construction of an RSX Program) 742 SB
1597 92 578 (CP/M 3 Programmer's Guide) 578 SB
