225 613 1777 (          The System Control Block \(SCB\) is a CP/M 3 data structure located in the BDOS.) 1777 SB
225 672 1702 (       CP/M 3 uses this region primarily for communication between the BDOS and the) 1702 SB
225 731 1695 (       BIOS.  However, it is also available for communication between application pro-) 1695 SB
225 790 1732 (       grams, RSXS, and the BDOS.  Note that programs that access the System Control) 1732 SB
225 849 1414 (       Block are not version independent.  They can run only on CP/M 3.) 1414 SB
225 968 1719 (          The following list describes the fields of the SCB that are available for access by) 1719 SB
225 1027 1773 (       application programs and RSXS.  The location of each field is described as the offset) 1773 SB
225 1086 1715 (       from the start address of the SCB \(see BDOS Function 49\).  The RW/RO column) 1715 SB
225 1145 1168 (       indicates if the SCB field is Read-Write or Read-Only.) 1168 SB
225 1264 1168 (                              Table A-1.  SCB Fields and Definitions) 1168 SB
225 1323 885 (           Offset   RW/RO                 Definition) 885 SB
225 1441 524 (         00 - 04       RO        ) 524 SB
825 1441 495 (Reserved for system use.) 495 SB
225 1559 535 (         05              RO         ) 535 SB
825 1559 489 (BDOS Version Number.) 489 SB
225 1678 456 (         06 - 09      RW   ) 456 SB
825 1678 1035 (Reserved for user use. Use these four bytes for your) 1035 SB
225 1737 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 1737 358 (own flags or data.) 358 SB
225 1855 285 (        0A - 0F  ) 285 SB
525 1855 212 (  RO         ) 212 SB
825 1855 495 (Reserved for system use.) 495 SB
225 1974 260 (       10 - 11  ) 260 SB
525 1974 222 (  RW         ) 222 SB
825 1974 1051 (Program Error Return Code. This 2-byte field can be) 1051 SB
225 2033 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 2033 1062 (used by a program to pass an error code or value to a) 1062 SB
225 2092 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 2092 1108 (chained program.  CP/M 3's conditional command facil-) 1108 SB
225 2151 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 2151 1040 (ity also uses this field to determine if a program exe-) 1040 SB
225 2210 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 2210 1071 (cutes successfully.  The BDOS Function 108 \(Get/Set) 1071 SB
225 2269 468 (                                    ) 468 SB
825 2269 1018 (Program Return Code\) is used to get/set this value.) 1018 SB
225 2388 273 (       12 - 19   ) 273 SB
525 2388 186 (RO         ) 186 SB
825 2388 495 (Reserved for system use.) 495 SB
1161 2861 77 (A-1) 77 SB
