225 1678 1617 (         The bit map is a string of bits identifying those bytes in the source code that) 1617 SB
225 1737 1772 (       require relocation.  There is one byte in the bit map for every 8 bytes of source code.) 1772 SB
225 1796 1705 (       The most significant bit, bit 7, of the first byte of the bit map indicates whether or) 1705 SB
225 1855 1736 (       not the first byte of the source code requires relocation.  If the bit is on, it indicates) 1736 SB
225 1914 1705 (       that relocation is required.  The next bit, bit 6, of the first byte corresponds to the) 1705 SB
