225 613 1745 (          System Page Relocatable, SPR, files are similar in format to PRL files except that) 1745 SB
225 672 1818 (        SPR files have an origin offset of 0000H \(see Appendix B\).  SPR Files are provided as) 1818 SB
225 731 1776 (        part of the standard CP/M 3 System: the resident and banked portions of the banked) 1776 SB
225 790 1791 (        BDOS, named RESBDOS3.SPR and BNKBDOS3.SPR, and the nonbanked BDOS,,) 1791 SB
225 849 1738 (        named BDOS3.SPR. The customized BIOS must also be generated in SPR format) 1738 SB
225 909 1624 (        before GENCPM can create a CP/M 3 system.  The BIOS SPR file is named) 1624 SB
225 968 1889 (        BNKBIOS3.SPR for banked systems and BIOS3.SPR for nonbanked systems.  A detailed) 1889 SB
225 1027 1752 (        discussion of the generation of BIOS3.SPR or BNK-BIOS3.SPR is provided in the) 1752 SB
225 1086 1367 (        CPIM Plus \(CP/M Version 3\) Operating System System Guide.) 1367 SB
225 1204 1749 (          The method of generating an SPR is analogous to that of generating a Page Relo-) 1749 SB
225 1264 1576 (        catable Program \(described in Appendix B\) with the following exceptions:) 1576 SB
225 1382 1756 (            o If LINK-80 is used, the output file of type SPR is specified with the [os] or [b]) 1756 SB
225 1441 1436 (               option.  The [b] option is used when linking BNKBIOS3.SPR.) 1436 SB
225 1559 1353 (            o Tne code in the SPR is ORGed at 000H rather than 100H.) 1353 SB
